PVD("egypt_vision_2016-2030",{"docs":["","EG Vision 2030"],"s":{"1":[[1,"9","3","Governance and Institutional Development Framework","The sixth and final strategic goal, «Governance and Partnerships>> embodies the comprehensive plan for institutional development under the rule of law.",""],[1,"14","6","Anti-Corruption and Transparency Governance Reform","The sixth strategic goal, \"Governance and Partnerships\" targets eliminating corruption, ensuring transparency, progressing towards strengthening international and local partnerships, and guaranteeing citizen participation in decision-making processes concerning development and their well-being at all levels.",""],[1,"168","1","Transparency and Anti-Corruption Reform","The strategic goal of\"Governance and Partnerships\" unfolds into seven general goals: \"Administrative reform\", \"Reinforcing Transparency and Combating Corruption\", \"Promoting Accountability and Responsibility\", \"Empowering Local Administration\", \"Strengthening Partnerships\", \"Enhancing Regional and International Cooperation\", and \"Preserving Stability and Security\".",""],[1,"170","5","Anti-Corruption Strategy Adoption","The state adoption of the Anti-Corruption Strategy in its first and second versions is a significant evidence of the state's desire to combat corruption in all its organizational, political, economic and social forms.",""],[1,"171","2","Transparency and Information Accessibility in Policymaking","Egypt's Vision 2030 aims to consolidate and strengthen the principle of transparency in policymaking.",""],[1,"171","2","National Anti-Corruption Strategy","This is affirmed by the pillars of the National Anti-Corruption Strategy, which provides effective frameworks to promote integrity, not only in public institutions, but also in private sector entities and civil society organizations.",""],[1,"172","1","Transparency and Disclosure Legislation Acceleration","Accelerating the issuance of laws that support transparency and disclosure.",""],[1,"172","2","Activation of Internal Audit Units","Activating internal audit units within the state administrative apparatus to limit corrupt practices.",""],[1,"172","3","Judicial System and Oversight Bodies Infrastructure and Technology Development","Completing the development of the infrastructure and technology of the judicial system and oversight bodies.",""],[1,"172","4","Anti-Corruption Awareness Campaigns","Increasing awareness campaigns that highlight the dangers of corruption, in collaboration with media and religious institutions.",""],[1,"172","4","Transparency and Anti-Corruption Capacity Enhancement","enhancing the efficiency of employees in the public and private sectors as well as civil society regarding transparency and anti-corruption efforts.",""],[1,"172","5","Anti-Corruption Curriculum Integration","Incorporating the concept of corruption, its forms, manifestations, and risks into educational curricula at various levels.",""],[1,"172","7","Listed Company Disclosure and Transparency Enforcement","Promoting and enforcing disclosure and transparency requirements for listed companies on the stock exchange.",""],[1,"172","8","Ethical and Professional Conduct Codes Implementation","Activating codes of ethical and professional conduct in both the public and private sectors.",""],[1,"172","11","Journalist Anti-Corruption Training Programme","Training journalists to uncover corrupt practices.",""]],"2":[[1,"14","6","Citizen Participation in Decision-Making Mechanism","The sixth strategic goal, \"Governance and Partnerships\" targets eliminating corruption, ensuring transparency, progressing towards strengthening international and local partnerships, and guaranteeing citizen participation in decision-making processes concerning development and their well-being at all levels.",""],[1,"14","6","Public-Private and Civil Society Partnership Strengthening","This involves assigning a bigger role to the private sector, civil society organizations, and associations, alongside the public sector, to enhance the satisfaction of each individual and ultimately benefit the human beings who are at the core of development.",""],[1,"37","4","Consultation and Societal Dialogue Mechanism","This is in addition to building a mechanism for consultation and societal dialogue with the concerned parties outside the decision-making process, to take into account different viewpoints when drafting new legislations or addressing legislative disparities.",""],[1,"38","6","Parliamentary Public Policy Alternatives Forum","The transformation of the Parliament into a forum for discussing \"Public Policy Alternatives\" to achieve SDGs.",""],[1,"43","3","Volunteer Work Promotion and Youth Awareness Programme","Promoting volunteer work to achieve inclusive development, as it can only be achieved through the coordination of state efforts and their integration with the entire society.",""],[1,"43","4","Government-Civil Society Coordination and Integration Mechanism","Effective coordination and integration between the GoE and the civil society play a significant role in clarifying societal needs and local variations.",""],[1,"55","1","Civil Society, Private Sector, and Government Coordination for Development Projects","Coordinate civil efforts through facilitating the collaboration between the private sector, civil society institutions, and the government to execute developmental projects effectively.",""],[1,"78","8","Local Development Partnership Coordination Framework","Strengthening institutional partnerships among local authorities, the private sector, and civil society; to set the developmental map for each governorate and agree on the distribution of roles and responsibilities thus ensuring the success of these partnerships.",""],[1,"165","3","Inclusive Governance and Accountability Framework","Therefore, the involvement of all relevant stakeholders in the decision-making process, both nationally and locally, within a legislative and institutional framework supporting transparency and accountability, is crucial.",""],[1,"170","3","Community Participation and Citizen Feedback Mechanisms","Establishing and activating mechanisms for community participation in policy development, while facilitating the evaluation of government performance through clear, announced, and electronic citizen complaint mechanisms, alongside feedback channels.",""],[1,"172","10","Civil Society Organization Efficiency Strengthening","Strengthening the efficiency of civil society organizations.",""],[1,"173","1","Legal Awareness Enhancement","and enhancing legal awareness among the majority of the population",""],[1,"173","1","Official and Social Accountability Systems","Additionally, it is reflected in implementing diverse forms of official and social accountability systems through oversight entities, to establish the foundations for a successful judicial system in Egypt.",""],[1,"174","2","Social Accountability Systems Development","Developing social accountability systems, such as participatory budgeting, monitoring government expenditures, and involving citizens in the planning process.",""],[1,"175","2","Participatory Local Decision-Making and Local Revenue Expansion","Furthermore, the state aims through this legal framework, to promote participatory local decision-making by supporting the tasks of local councils.",""],[1,"176","6","Local Complaint Mechanisms Reinforcement","Reinforcing local complaint mechanisms.",""],[1,"178","3","Civil Society Monitoring, Awareness, and Capacity-Building Partnership","Civil society's role extends beyond voluntary and charitable contributions. It is crucial in monitoring, raising awareness, and capacity-building.",""],[1,"186","6","Counter-Extremist Rhetoric and Tolerance Education Initiative","Intellectually combating extremist rhetoric through a revitalized religious discourse, raising awareness to counter extremist ideologies, and incorporating values of tolerance and acceptance of others into educational curricula.",""]],"3":[[1,"25","2","Digital Governance and Administrative Reform Support","Both global and local technological platforms play a key role in stimulating participatory approaches, supporting administrative reforms, improving the efficiency and effectiveness of government agencies, enhancing governance, and achieving stability on both domestic and international fronts.",""],[1,"28","5","Digital Transformation Enablement Framework","Strengthening digital transformation is a key enabler that contributes to achieving all the goals outlined in Egypt's Vision 2030, be it economic, social, institutional, or environmental.",""],[1,"29","1","Digital Transformation for Service Delivery and Governance","Ultimately, digital transformation plays a role in reducing transaction costs and enhancing institutional governance.",""],[1,"29","6","Electronic Government Services Portal","An electronic government services portal has been launched, offering services such as supply, real estate, documentation, civil status, and vehicle licensing.",""],[1,"29","7","Expansion of Digital Transformation Centers and Citizen Services","The expansion in digital transformation projects and the development of services to citizens have been achieved through the development of technological centers in neighborhoods and cities.",""],[1,"31","3","Digital Transformation of Government Institutions","The aim is for digital transformation to improve the effectiveness of government institutions in fulfilling the citizens' needs, rendering them more transparent and inclusive, while also offering new tools and opportunities to address crises and surmount developmental obstacles.",""],[1,"75","2","Digital Transformation for Basic Services and Subsidy Targeting","\"Digital Transformation\" that facilitate citizens' access to basic services and improve the subsidies system, particularly targeting and strengthening communication channels between all societal segments;",""],[1,"121","1","Digital Transformation and Services Automation Initiative","Encouraging digital transformation, services automation, and data accessibility.",""],[1,"158","2","Unified Beneficiary Information System","institutional efforts are underway to establish a unified information system encompassing accurate and periodic data and statistics on the beneficiaries of all services, including education, health, transportation, and supply",""],[1,"158","2","National Digital Transformation Coordination Bodies","the National Payments Council and the Supreme Council of Digital Society were established to support the government's transition to a unified mechanism for digital transformation for achieving integration between databases and facilitating the provision of automated services to citizens and different entities",""],[1,"158","2","Electronic Government Payments and Procurement Systems","the electronic government payments system and the electronic government procurement and contracting system were launched to simplify contracting procedures and promote transparency between government entities and the business community",""],[1,"158","2","Governorate Technology Centers","technology centers were established in the governorates to facilitate services delivery to citizens",""],[1,"158","2","Public Service Automation for Social Protection Targeting","the automation of public services played a crucial role in enhancing the efficiency and effectiveness of targeting recipients eligible for subsidies under social protection programs",""],[1,"170","1","Unified Automated Digital Transformation System","Finalizing the unified automated system for digital transformation and continuously enhancing the electronic system, to foster seamless connectivity between the databases of various government entities.",""],[1,"170","2","State Resource Management Systems Enhancement","Enhancing and developing state resource management systems to optimize government expenditure efficiency.",""],[1,"170","4","Government Cloud Computing and Artificial Intelligence Systems","Provide funding for implementing advanced systems that enable the utilization of cloud computing and artificial intelligence in government operations.",""],[1,"172","6","Automated Investor Services System","Automating investor services to ensure corruption-free transactions.",""]],"4":[[1,"27","2","Scientific Research Legal and Regulatory Reform","Supporting scientific research legislation by updating laws, legislation and regulations governing the management of the scientific research process and policies, as well as supporting intellectual property issues and professional standards, and broadening the application of various incentives.",""],[1,"27","3","Scientific Research Institutional Framework Development","Developing the institutional system for scientific research and formulating an effective organizational structure that clearly defines responsibilities and interrelationships among all stakeholders involved in scientific research",""],[1,"27","3","Technology Incubators and Innovation Parks Establishment","encouraging the establishment of technological incubators and innovation parks within research institutions across cities and regions",""],[1,"27","4","Alignment of Scientific Research and University Theses with Economic Needs","Setting scientific research priorities and guiding university theses and research towards specialized applied fields that align with the needs of the Egyptian economy, while considering social and environmental objectives, in return for receiving support from production sectors.",""],[1,"27","5","Private Sector and Research Center Collaboration for Specialized Research Centers","Encouraging the private sector and chambers of industry and commerce to collaborate with government research centers in establishing specialized research centers.",""],[1,"27","6","Research Funding Diversification and Partnership Expansion","Diversifying the funding sources for scientific research by strengthening partnerships with technologically advanced countries, international financing institutions, and entities supporting scientific research both within and outside of Egypt.",""],[1,"27","7","Innovation Financing Programs","Developing and introducing new financing programs with the participation of the private sector, research entities, and all development partners to stimulate innovation, particularly in the field of fundamental sciences and the development of Egyptian products.",""],[1,"63","3","Research Center Establishment and Scientific Research Support","Providing financial support to establish research centers, and expanding scientific research in various fields.",""],[1,"63","6","Continuous Evaluation of Scientific Research Institutions","Conducting continuous evaluations of scientific research institutions and centers and developing local evaluation criteria that consider their contribution to the implementation of Egypt's Vision 2030.",""],[1,"63","7","Scientific Personnel Mobility Reform","Revising recruitment laws and university regulations to facilitate the mobility of scientific personnel.",""],[1,"118","10","Science-to-Industry Innovation Linkage","Bridging scientific research with developmental sectors to foster innovative and creative production methods.",""],[1,"118","10","Knowledge and Innovation Commercialization Initiative","converting knowledge and innovation into high-value economic products or services.",""],[1,"123","6","Research and Development Investment Expansion","Increasing public expenditure on research and development while leveraging the outcomes of research and studies.",""],[1,"123","7","Business-Academia Partnership for Innovation and Labor Market Linkages","Supporting partnerships between the business sector and academic institutions to harness academic innovations, thereby positively influencing the labor market.",""],[1,"124","1","Intellectual Property Institutional and Legislative Support","Supporting the institutional and legislative environment for intellectual property and encouraging patents.",""],[1,"124","2","Engagement with Egyptian Scientists Abroad","Increasing collaboration and connections with Egyptian scientists abroad to tap into their wealth of expertise.",""],[1,"129","8","Innovation Incentive and Financing Support for Young Talent","Promoting innovation by encouraging new ideas and offering incentive and financing packages to support young talents, and aligning sector needs with innovative and creative solutions for industrial challenges.",""]],"5":[[1,"9","1","Labor Market Efficiency and Workforce Skills Enhancement","These efforts are part of a broader framework aimed at enhancing labor market efficiency, elevating the skills and proficiency of the Egyptian workforce, boosting competitiveness, fostering innovation, and transitioning towards a cashless society.",""],[1,"13","2","Education, Training, and Skills Refinement for Future Jobs","Egypt's Vision 2030 seeks to improve the living standards of all segments of society by ensuring access to quality education, training, and skill refinement necessary for future job prospects grounded in scientific research and innovation, along with providing adequate health insurance.",""],[1,"36","6","Job Creation Measures","creating job opportunities",""],[1,"122","3","Education and Skills Investment for Knowledge Economy Development","This, in turn, necessitates increased investment in education, raising the qualifications of graduates of technical schools and universities, and expanding vocational training to supply skilled workers equipped for new jobs, thus contributing to the provision of decent employment opportunities.",""],[1,"123","3","Labor Market-Aligned Curriculum Development","Enhancing the efficiency of the educational process by developing programs and curricula that closely align with the dynamic needs of the labor market.",""],[1,"123","4","Human Capital and Technological Skills Development","Supporting investment in human capital and developing technological skills in accordance with the latest educational and vocational systems.",""],[1,"123","5","Private Sector and Civil Society Participation in Vocational Training","Encouraging the contribution of the private sector and civil society in enhancing the vocational training system's efficiency.",""],[1,"124","3","International Accreditation of Certificates and Professional Qualifications","facilitating international accreditation of certificates and professional qualifications for Egyptians seeking work abroad.",""],[1,"133","6","SME Worker Professional Training Programme","Providing professional training for workers in SMEs, including those in the informal sector, to support these enterprises, enhance their productivity, and improve their working conditions.",""]],"6":[[1,"9","2","Communication and Information Systems Development","Additionally, it entails developing communication and information systems to foster an appealing investment environment that supports public-private partnerships in infrastructure projects, and to construct an advanced industrial base that enhances the competitiveness of the national economy.",""],[1,"31","4","Digital Infrastructure Expansion Across All Regions","Developing digital infrastructure across all geographical regions, especially in remote areas.",""],[1,"31","5","Digital Infrastructure Investment","Encouraging investments in digital infrastructure to meet present and future demands, and address digital divides.",""],[1,"142","3","Advanced Digital Infrastructure Development","the strategic implementation of major projects in communications, information technology, and both submarine and terrestrial cables",""],[1,"143","3","Digital Transformation and Innovation for Service Delivery","In addition, \"technology and innovation\" that calls for embracing modern sciences, such as using artificial intelligence and the green economy to provide essential services and \"digital transformation\" that supports the automation and accessibility of services while enhancing their quality.",""],[1,"157","4","Digital Infrastructure Investment","investing in digital infrastructure has a favorable impact on the business environment.",""],[1,"157","4","Public Service Digitalization and Automation","This, in turn, results in reduced transaction costs, integration and automation of public services, and connecting the government, private sector, and civil society, ultimately leading to cost reduction and quality enhancement in services.",""],[1,"157","4","Digital Resource Management and Complaints Mechanism","Furthermore, digitizing resource management and providing a digital mechanism for complaints and responses enhance institutional efficiency and foster accountability.",""],[1,"160","1","National Internet Connectivity Expansion","it aims to achieve significant progress and widespread adoption of information technology systems by connecting all geographical regions to the internet and its related services.",""],[1,"160","2","Affordable Internet Access Expansion","Achieving digital equity through providing affordable internet services across all geographic regions.",""],[1,"160","3","Government Employee ICT Best Practices Training","Training government employees on best information and communication technology practices.",""],[1,"160","6","Global Data Center Investment Attraction and Regional Data Hub Development","Attracting global data centers for investment and working towards positioning Egypt as a regional hub for data and knowledge exchange, using artificial intelligence.",""]],"7":[[1,"9","1","Business Climate Improvement and Informal Economy Formalization","This is achieved through improving the business climate, enhancing competitiveness, and formalizing the informal economy.",""],[1,"36","6","Investment Facilitation and Regulatory Liberalization","addressing conditions or decisions that do not support development and require facilitation or liberation to encourage investment",""],[1,"37","4","ERRADA Initiative Revitalization","Revitalizing the \"ERRADA\" initiative, which is a unit under the presidency of the Council of Ministers pursuant to the Prime Minister Resolution No. 998 of 2019.",""],[1,"37","4","Legislative and Procedural Business Environment Reform","It aims to contribute to reforming the legislative and procedural system regulating the business environment, as well as building a legislative impact assessment system to support decision-makers in regulating the practice of economic activities.",""],[1,"38","4","Legislative Framework for Sustainable Development and Regulatory Reform","The aim is to build a legislative framework to support sustainable development efforts with the speed and efficiency necessary to improve performance and review all laws, implementing regulations, and ministerial decisions issued, to achieve structural reform, regulate the practice of economic activities, create a business climate, and support fair competition policies.",""],[1,"39","6","Business Environment Legislative Reform and Database Initiative","Seek guidance from the \"ERRADA\" initiative, which focuses on reforming the legislative system regulating the business environment and building a database of legislations that regulate the business environment, in a way that enables the implementation of similar initiatives in other sectors, such as social and service fields (health, education and transportation ... etc.).",""],[1,"114","2","Investment Attraction and Competitiveness Support","The state commits to protecting them, increasing their competitiveness, providing an environment that attracts investment, and works on increasing production, encouraging exports, and regulating imports",""],[1,"114","4","Private Sector Empowerment and Enabling Environment Reform","This involves the government providing robust infrastructure, enhancing the legislative environment,",""],[1,"115","1","Informal Sector Formalization Incentive Package","Additionally, integrating the informal sector into the formal economy by offering various incentives, including facilitating access to financing, fostering innovation, and raising awareness of non-cash transactions.",""],[1,"119","1","Business Climate Support and Investment Promotion","it becomes imperative to support the business climate to foster competitiveness, enhance market efficiency, promote economic flexibility, create more employment opportunities, support existing investments, and attract both domestic and foreign investments.",""],[1,"120","1","Investment Service Centers and Automated Investor Services","The establishment of investment service centers across different governorates, coupled with automated services, reflect a proactive effort to streamline procedures for investors.",""]],"8":[[1,"45","3","Executive Plan for the National Project for the Development of the Egyptian Family","The GoE has initiated the implementation of the Executive Plan for the National Project for the Development of the Egyptian Family (2021/2022 - 2023/2024), focusing on two main aspects: controlling population growth and enhancing population characteristics in education, health, job opportunities, economic empowerment, and culture.",""],[1,"45","3","Women's Economic Empowerment Initiative","The plan revolves around five pillars: Women's Economic Empowerment; Availability of Family Planning Methods; Cultural, Media, and Educational Interventions to raise awareness about the population issue; Utilizing Digital Transformation to reach the targeted population; and Legislative Interventions to establish a comprehensive framework for population-related policies.",""],[1,"45","3","Family Planning Access Expansion","The plan revolves around five pillars: Women's Economic Empowerment; Availability of Family Planning Methods; Cultural, Media, and Educational Interventions to raise awareness about the population issue; Utilizing Digital Transformation to reach the targeted population; and Legislative Interventions to establish a comprehensive framework for population-related policies.",""],[1,"45","3","Population Awareness Campaigns","The plan revolves around five pillars: Women's Economic Empowerment; Availability of Family Planning Methods; Cultural, Media, and Educational Interventions to raise awareness about the population issue; Utilizing Digital Transformation to reach the targeted population; and Legislative Interventions to establish a comprehensive framework for population-related policies.",""],[1,"45","3","Digital Outreach for Population Targeting","The plan revolves around five pillars: Women's Economic Empowerment; Availability of Family Planning Methods; Cultural, Media, and Educational Interventions to raise awareness about the population issue; Utilizing Digital Transformation to reach the targeted population; and Legislative Interventions to establish a comprehensive framework for population-related policies.",""],[1,"45","3","Population Policy Legislative Framework","The plan revolves around five pillars: Women's Economic Empowerment; Availability of Family Planning Methods; Cultural, Media, and Educational Interventions to raise awareness about the population issue; Utilizing Digital Transformation to reach the targeted population; and Legislative Interventions to establish a comprehensive framework for population-related policies.",""],[1,"75","2","Population Growth Control","\"Population Growth Control\" helps maximize the benefits of development.",""],[1,"143","3","Population Growth Management","\"population growth control\" to strike a balance between development and population growth.",""]],"9":[[1,"99","4","Combined-Cycle Power Plant Expansion","Electricity production witnessed continuous growth after the introduction of new combined- cycle power plants, the enhancement of power generator efficiency through natural gas, and the increased utilization of renewable energy sources such as solar and wind power, both in electricity production and seawater desalination.",""],[1,"99","4","Renewable Energy Expansion for Power and Desalination","Electricity production witnessed continuous growth after the introduction of new combined- cycle power plants, the enhancement of power generator efficiency through natural gas, and the increased utilization of renewable energy sources such as solar and wind power, both in electricity production and seawater desalination.",""],[1,"99","4","Hydroelectric Potential Utilization and New Energy Feasibility Studies","This in addition to the nearly full exploitation of hydroelectric energy potential and exploring the feasibility of incorporating various new energy sources like hydrogen (blue and green).",""],[1,"144","2","National Electricity Infrastructure Upgrade and Expansion","A comprehensive enhancement of the electricity infrastructure unfolded across the nation, interconnecting regions of production and distribution with those of storage and consumption.",""],[1,"144","2","Power Generation Station Construction and Grid Reinforcement","New stations were established, and transmission and distribution networks underwent significant upgrades and fortification.",""],[1,"144","2","Fuel Diversification and Electricity Resource Exploration","The sources of fuel for electricity production were diversified, coupled with improved investments in research and exploration to augment reserves and amplify production.",""]],"10":[[1,"16","3","Resilience and Adaptability Framework","the vision places the principle of \"Resilience and Adaptability\" as a foundation that supports the level of readiness and raises it in emergencies.",""],[1,"16","3","International Partnership and Private Sector Engagement for Resilience","these measures necessitate bolstering international partnerships to draw from experiences, whether for technical assistance or financing, alongside efforts to encourage private sector involvement due to its rapid adaptability and integration across all productive sectors.",""],[1,"95","2","National Climate Change Strategy 2050","Egypt launched in 2021 the National Climate Change Strategy 2050, which serves as the guiding framework for addressing the adverse consequences of climate change.",""],[1,"95","3","Climate Change Adaptation and Mitigation Measures","This includes implementing essential measures, offering ecosystem services, and establishing financing mechanisms to effectively monitor and mitigate the impact on natural resources, coastal regions, and biodiversity.",""],[1,"95","4","Climate Change Institutional Capacity Building","Supporting institutional development, capacity building, and technical expertise enhancement in the field of climate change.",""],[1,"95","4","Environmental Department Skills Development","developing skilled personnel and technical expertise in environmental departments across the governorates.",""],[1,"96","2","National Extreme Weather Impact Monitoring Program","Formulate a national program to monitor the impacts of extreme weather events and their negative effects on sectors vulnerable to climate change.",""],[1,"96","4","Integration of Environmental and Climate Standards into National Planning","Integrating environmental standards and measures related to climate change into national policies, strategies, and development plans.",""],[1,"96","5","National Climate Change Adaptation Planning","Preparing national plans to adapt to climate change, especially in the agriculture, water resources, and integrated coastal resource management sectors, in addition to formulating a low-emissions development strategy.",""],[1,"96","6","Climate Adaptation Projects for Vulnerable Coastal and Agricultural Areas","Expanding the implementation of adaptation projects in the most vulnerable sectors, such as safeguarding beaches and low-lying areas in the Nile Delta.",""],[1,"96","6","Climate-Resilient Agriculture and Water Reuse Measures","cultivating crops resistant to drought, soil deficiencies, salinity, and temperature, recycling water, and utilizing non-traditional water sources.",""],[1,"96","7","Climate-Resilient Infrastructure Support","Prioritizing support for infrastructure in areas most vulnerable to adverse effects of climate change.",""],[1,"96","8","Climate Risk Mapping and Early Warning System","Activating interactive maps of climate change risks, threats, and expected impacts across various sectors and regions.",""],[1,"97","1","University and Research Center Agricultural Innovation Support","Enhancing the role of universities and research centers in developing agricultural methods that target climate-adaptive crops and water conservation techniques.",""],[1,"97","3","Climate Change Public Awareness and Community Participation Initiative","Raising public awareness about the risks and impacts of climate change.",""],[1,"97","3","Local Community Involvement in Emissions Reduction Policy Development","In addition to, involving local communities - at both the individual and institutional level - in the development and implementation of policies to reduce greenhouse gas emissions.",""],[1,"146","4","Rainwater Harvesting and Floodwater Collection Projects in Sinai","Around 200 projects aimed at harvesting rainwater and floods in Sinai have been established, along with artificial ground reservoirs and dams, to collect precipitation.",""],[1,"147","2","Coastal Seawater Desalination Plant Expansion","Seawater desalination plants have been expanded in coastal regions with a high concentration on resorts and tourist villages, capitalizing on Egypt's extensive coastline spanning approximately 2,400 kilometers.",""],[1,"147","2","Private Sector Participation in Desalination","By motivating private sector participation and encouraging the implementation of desalination plants, it is projected that an extra 650 million cubic meters of desalinated water can be added to the water balance, ultimately reaching 1 billion cubic meters by 2030.",""],[1,"149","2","Groundwater Resource Optimization Plan","Implementing a comprehensive plan to optimize the use of available groundwater, preserving this vital source for the benefit of future generations.",""],[1,"185","4","Water Resource Expansion and Reuse Programme","Strengthening the current water resources with new resources to bridge the gap between local production and actual needs.",""]],"11":[[1,"165","2","Governance Institutional and Legislative Reform","Implementing these principles necessitates multifaceted reforms, encompassing institutional and legislative aspects.",""],[1,"165","2","Human Capacity and Organizational Culture Strengthening","A pivotal facet involves enhancing human capacities and transforming organizational culture and behavior.",""],[1,"168","1","Administrative Reform","The strategic goal of\"Governance and Partnerships\" unfolds into seven general goals: \"Administrative reform\", \"Reinforcing Transparency and Combating Corruption\", \"Promoting Accountability and Responsibility\", \"Empowering Local Administration\", \"Strengthening Partnerships\", \"Enhancing Regional and International Cooperation\", and \"Preserving Stability and Security\".",""],[1,"168","1","Local Administration Empowerment","The strategic goal of\"Governance and Partnerships\" unfolds into seven general goals: \"Administrative reform\", \"Reinforcing Transparency and Combating Corruption\", \"Promoting Accountability and Responsibility\", \"Empowering Local Administration\", \"Strengthening Partnerships\", \"Enhancing Regional and International Cooperation\", and \"Preserving Stability and Security\".",""],[1,"168","2","Administrative Reform and Accountability Strengthening Plan","To this end, the state has placed considerable emphasis on administrative reform by developing a comprehensive plan that targets the establishment of an efficient and productive administrative structure, which is accountable through effective monitoring and evaluation systems.",""],[1,"169","2","Administrative Reform Plan","Accordingly, the pillars of the administrative reform plan are designed to create a legislative framework that balances discipline and flexibility within government bodies, enhances the capabilities of state employees, and optimizes the data and information system.",""],[1,"169","3","Administrative Law and Regulation Consolidation Review","Consolidate all laws and regulations governing the state's administrative apparatus.",""],[1,"169","5","Public Administration Restructuring Reform","Undertaking a comprehensive restructuring of the state's administrative apparatus to enhance effectiveness and accountability, and address issues related to overlapping responsibilities.",""],[1,"169","6","Public Sector Human Resource Capacity Building","Developing human resources by building the capacities of personnel and administrative leaders within the state's administrative apparatus.",""],[1,"173","1","Update Fundamental Laws","Consequently, the importance of this goal manifests in updating fundamental laws",""],[1,"174","3","Strengthening Accountability of Local Executive Authorities","Strengthening accountability measures for local executive authorities through elected local councils.",""],[1,"174","6","Local Governance Legal and Institutional Reform","The process of empowering local administration involves the development of the legal framework for the local governance system, which divides functions and activities between the central and local levels in a consistent manner.",""],[1,"174","6","Local Administration Capacity Building and Institutional Restructuring","Capacity building, along with the restructuring of administrative and functional aspects of both central and local institutions, in accordance with their new mandates, are integral to this process.",""],[1,"174","6","Local Planning, Financing, and Financial Control Systems","This includes the development of local planning and financing systems, alongside supporting financial control mechanisms at both the central and local levels.",""],[1,"175","2","State General Planning Law for Local Development Planning","the state has worked on preparing a legal framework the \"State's General Planning Law\", to empower local units to develop their developmental plans and sustainable development reports that identify developmental gaps.",""],[1,"175","2","Local Planning Flexibility and Resource Mobilization Framework","It also aims at granting local units greater freedom and flexibility in implementing these plans, while encouraging the mobilization of additional resources, and directing them towards developmental investment projects.",""],[1,"176","1","Governorate Financing Formula for Public Investment Allocation","the \"Financing Formula\" for governorates seeks fair and objective distribution of public investments among them, considering the distinct social and economic characteristics and conditions of each, while acknowledging a non-uniform set of benchmark criteria.",""],[1,"176","2","Local Administration Empowerment and Decentralization Reform","Egypt's Vision 2030 strives to empower local administration by granting it greater decision-making authority and focusing on the comparative advantages of each governorate.",""],[1,"176","3","Equitable Regional Investment Allocation","Ensuring equitable allocation of investments - particularly those from the government - across diverse geographical regions.",""],[1,"176","4","Local Administration Empowerment and Capacity Strengthening","Adopting a gradual strategy that empowers local administration and enhances local human and institutional capacities.",""],[1,"176","5","Local Accountability and Oversight Mechanisms","Improving infrastructure and information technology and establishing mechanisms for local accountability and oversight while amending local institutional frameworks.",""],[1,"176","7","Intergovernmental Fiscal Transfer System","Empowering local administrations financially and establishing a system for intergovernmental fiscal transfers based on various indicators, such as population and poverty rates.",""]],"12":[[1,"6","3","National Forecasting and Contingency Preparedness","improving forecasting to anticipate any updates on the national, regional and global levels and prepare for any contingencies.",""],[1,"6","3","Economic Shock Resilience Strengthening","strengthening the ability of the economy to confront external shocks (for example, the outbreak of COVID-19 and the ensuing global economic downturn).",""]],"13":[[1,"8","4","Circular and Green Economy Promotion","It promotes the adoption of innovative economic models, including circular and green economies, to decouple economic growth from excessive reliance on natural resources, minimize resource waste and consumption, and create new green- collar jobs.",""],[1,"17","4","Green Economy Transition","This involves transitioning towards a green economy, ensuring low-emission economic growth by enhancing resource efficiency and promoting sustainable production and consumption patterns.",""],[1,"17","4","Circular Economy Implementation","Additionally, the implementation of a circular economy is encouraged to maximize the utilization of all production outputs, including secondary ones, by resource sharing, recycling, and waste conversion to enhance resource efficiency.",""]],"14":[[1,"9","1","Cashless Society Transition Framework","These efforts are part of a broader framework aimed at enhancing labor market efficiency, elevating the skills and proficiency of the Egyptian workforce, boosting competitiveness, fostering innovation, and transitioning towards a cashless society.",""],[1,"24","3","Innovative Financing Tools for Financial Inclusion","Utilizing technology and supporting financial inclusion by providing a diverse set of innovative financing tools, integrating all segments of society into the financial system, including the informal sector and those not willing to engage with the traditional banking system.",""]],"15":[[1,"9","2","Basic Services and Infrastructure Development","It underscores the importance of establishing secure and sustainable transportation systems, be it through the Suez Canal as a waterway, the utilization of electric traction within the railway network, or the development of a comprehensive network of roads, bridges, ports, and airports.",""]],"16":[[1,"14","3","Integrated Environmental Resource Management","It involves the conservation of biodiversity, the efficient management of waste, and the protection of natural resources and the environment in a way that upholds equitable utilization and safeguards the rights of future generations.",""],[1,"92","1","Environmental Protection and Sustainable Resource Use Measures","The state is committed to taking the necessary measures to preserve it, avoid harming it, rationally use its natural resources to ensure that sustainable development is achieved, and guarantee the rights of future generations thereto",""]],"17":[[1,"15","4","Equitable Delivery of Social Services and Opportunities","\"Equity and Accessibility\" involves delivering high-quality educational, training, healthcare, and infrastructure services, along with opportunities for decent and productive employment and social security, in an equitable manner to all segments of society irrespective of income levels, gender, age, or geographical location.",""],[1,"15","5","Inclusive High-Quality Service Delivery","This is accomplished by making various services available to them inclusively, and with high quality.",""],[1,"54","3","Inclusive Development and Social Inclusion Framework","This will be achieved within a framework of geographical justice through an inclusive developmental system, focusing on investing in human capital while adopting social inclusion to ensure the success of sustainable development.",""],[1,"82","1","Inclusion and Equal Opportunities Initiative","Consequently, a societal transformation is needed to enhance greater inclusion and activate a larger role for more social, economic, and political participation, especially for vulnerable groups, including women, children, youth, persons with disabilities, and the elderly.",""]],"18":[[1,"15","5","Women's Economic, Social, and Political Empowerment Initiative","The vision seeks to achieve its strategic goals in a manner that ensures gender equality by empowering women economically, socially, and politically.",""],[1,"36","6","Women Empowerment Incentives and Privileges","introducing incentives and privileges in other sectors to empower women",""],[1,"79","1","Women's Empowerment and Gender Equality Measures","Achieving social justice is closely interlinked with the genuine pursuit of gender equality, supporting equal opportunities, and enhancing women's participation in the development process leading to empowering women economically, socially, and politically.",""],[1,"80","3","Women's Empowerment and Gender Gap Reduction Initiative","Egypt's Vision 2030 aims to narrow the gender gap by empowering women to actively participate in all social, cultural, economic, and political aspects.",""],[1,"80","3","Women's Workforce Participation Promotion","The Vision emphasizes women's involvement in the workforce, enhanced political empowerment, reduction of female illiteracy rates, and provision of healthcare specifically for women in rural areas.",""],[1,"80","4","Gender Equality Awareness and Norm Change Campaign","Raise awareness of the risks of gender-based discrimination against women, change prevailing negative cultural norms and perceptions regarding frequent childbearing, early marriage, and limited access to education for girls in various regions of Egypt.",""],[1,"80","5","Women's Employment Access and Flexible Work Measures","Facilitate women's access to job opportunities, enhance mechanisms for home-based work and flexible working hours, and develop codes of conduct in collaboration with the private sector to",""],[1,"81","1","Safe Work Environment for Women Initiative","provide a safe work environment free from all forms of violence and discrimination against women.",""],[1,"81","2","Care Economy Development Initiative","Develop the care economy as a facilitator for women's employment, creating new job opportunities and allowing a balance between their productive and social roles.",""],[1,"81","3","Women’s SME Financing and Financial Inclusion Support","Provide funding with lenient conditions and guarantees for women to establish small and medium-sized projects, and financial literacy through financial inclusion programs for women in rural and remote areas.",""],[1,"81","4","Support for Female Entrepreneurs and Business Incubators","Provide technical support for female entrepreneurs, and establish business incubators for small and micro-projects.",""],[1,"81","5","Women's Skills Training Expansion Programme","Expand training programs to enhance women's skills in industries required in the job market, as well as in technological and digital fields to increase women's future job opportunities.",""],[1,"81","6","Women's Participation in Decision-Making Initiative","Enhance women's participation in decision-making processes at both the central and local governments.",""],[1,"81","7","Women's Shelters Development","Develop women's shelters to protect them from all forms of violence and abuse.",""],[1,"81","8","Elimination of Harmful Practices Against Girls","Eliminate harmful practices against girls (FGM and child marriage) by enforcing laws and raising awareness in all educational, cultural, media, and religious institutions.",""],[1,"81","9","Maternal Healthcare and Reproductive Health Awareness","Provide healthcare for women during pregnancy and raise awareness of the importance of family planning and reproductive health.",""],[1,"81","10","Gender Gap Incentive Information Dissemination","Promote accurate and effective dissemination of information regarding incentive measures available to governmental and non-governmental institutions to bridge the gender gap and enhance women's empowerment.",""]],"19":[[1,"21","1","Vision Financing Mobilization Mechanism","Financing is the primary tool for any implementation steps to fulfil the growing development needs.",""],[1,"21","2","Strategic Financing Framework for Development Goals","Securing funding requires a sustainable increase in available resources to better meet the requirements of development.",""],[1,"21","2","Incentives for Financing Social Protection and Development Sectors","This agenda adopted a new and binding framework for each country to establish a set of appropriate incentives that facilitate financing in vital areas of development, including social protection (poverty reduction, education, health, adequate food and housing), alongside infrastructure, scientific research, technology, digitization, capacity building, investment, and partnerships with the private sector and international institutions.",""],[1,"21","3","Diversified Development Financing Mobilization","Financing sources should not be limited to government expenditure or external funding through loans and official development assistance alone; they should also encompass private sector investments, contributions from civil society organizations, Foreign Direct Investments (FDIs), and local banking and non-banking institutions.",""],[1,"21","3","Innovative Financing Instruments Exploration","Additionally, new forms of financing, including innovative financial instruments like green bonds and others, should be explored.",""],[1,"24","1","Diversified Financing Mobilization Framework","The aim is for the state to stimulate diverse financing sources, eliminate barriers, and promote unconventional methods to bridge financing gaps, with the objective of realizing Egypt's Vision 2030 within a framework of transparency.",""],[1,"24","2","Local Financial Resource Mobilization Reform","Raising the efficiency of mobilizing local financial resources by raising awareness of the importance of saving values, rationalizing expenditure, stimulating the private sector to participate, and improving the tax system, to ensure effective access for all categories of financiers.",""],[1,"24","4","Private Sector and Civil Society Partnership and Communication Framework","Building strong partnerships and maintaining effective and continuous communication with the private sector and civil society by easing restrictions, reducing bureaucracy, enhancing the business environment, and creating an incentive system supporting the direction of private financing flows toward priorities and national goals.",""],[1,"24","5","Administrative and Procedural Governance Improvement for Development Financing","Continuously improving the governance of the administrative and procedural system to secure developmental financing, and maximize the benefits from the available funds.",""],[1,"24","6","Remittance Mobilization and Development Channeling Mechanism","Developing clear policies and mechanisms to support external flows and their mobilization, especially remittances from Egyptians working abroad, and directing them towards development.",""]],"20":[[1,"22","2","COVID-19 Economic Stimulus Packages","In response, the Government of Egypt (GoE) implemented a series of stimulus packages to mitigate the adverse effects of the pandemic on economic activities.",""],[1,"22","2","Loan Repayment Deferral for Small and Micro-Projects","Measures included deferring loan repayments for small and micro-projects, waiving certain sovereign fees, as well as expanding social protection networks to include irregular workers.",""],[1,"22","2","Credit Facilities for Essential and Strategic Commodities","These measures included the provision of necessary credit facilities to meet the requirements for essential and strategic commodities.",""],[1,"22","2","Private Sector Financing Initiative","Initiatives were launched to finance private sector companies in industrial, agricultural, and contracting fields.",""],[1,"22","2","Low-Interest MSME Financing Initiative","Additionally, an initiative was introduced to finance Micro-, Small and Medium-sized Enterprises (MSMEs) with low-interest rates and favorable terms.",""]],"21":[[1,"22","2","Expansion of Social Protection Networks for Irregular Workers","Measures included deferring loan repayments for small and micro-projects, waiving certain sovereign fees, as well as expanding social protection networks to include irregular workers.",""]],"22":[[1,"28","1","Talent Exploration Centers Revitalization and Gifted Student Support","revitalizing centers for talents exploration and enhancing the system for identifying and nurturing gifted and talented students in schools",""],[1,"28","1","Youth Creativity Competitions and Incentive Scheme","launching competitions, offering incentive initiatives, and awarding prizes for the best creative ideas",""],[1,"28","2","Innovation Talent Support Fund","Establishing a fund to nurture talented individuals, especially in the field of innovation, with the participation of both the private sector and the state, to support and promote new productive ideas and emerging projects and their products.",""],[1,"28","3","Diaspora Knowledge Transfer and Engagement Initiative","Making use of the exceptional expertise and skills of scholars and Egyptians residing abroad to transfer knowledge and connect them with their home country.",""],[1,"68","11","Talent Discovery and Nurturing Programme","Discover and nurture talented, gifted, creative, and innovative individuals to build the human capital that empowers Egypt to achieve regional and global leadership and competition in various fields of scientific, literary, artistic, cultural, and sports creativity.",""]],"23":[[1,"30","1","E-Learning Infrastructure Support in Schools and Universities","Support for e-learning in schools and universities has been strengthened by providing devices, equipment, and programs to develop the necessary infrastructure.",""],[1,"31","9","Digital Literacy and Education Enrollment Expansion","Reducing overall illiteracy rates, especially digital illiteracy, and increasing enrollment rates in all levels of education to equip citizens with essential digital skills.",""],[1,"32","1","Specialized Colleges in Artificial Intelligence and Biotechnology","Expanding the establishment of specialized colleges in artificial intelligence and biotechnology, that use curricula aligned with the Fourth Industrial Revolution (4IR).",""],[1,"32","2","ICT Sector Human Resource Training Programme","Broadening training programs to enhance the efficiency of human resources operating in the ICT sector.",""],[1,"32","3","Digital Economy Promotion Initiative","Promoting the digital economy as a value-added component in the national economy, accommodating various categories of the unemployed workforce, providing opportunities for professional mobility, and empowering women economically through flexible work arrangements, that help achieve a work-family balance.",""],[1,"32","4","Digital Inclusion Support for Women and Persons with Disabilities","Supporting women and persons with disabilities in using communications and information technologies, promoting the use of electronic applications in various fields such as health and education.",""],[1,"36","2","Data Handling and Advanced Systems Capacity Building","Enhancing capacities and skills in data handling and utilizing advanced systems.",""]],"24":[[1,"31","6","Data Protection and User Privacy Regulatory Framework","Setting clear legislations and regulations to ensure the maintenance of data protection and user privacy.",""],[1,"31","7","Information Technology Market Competition Enforcement","Promoting competition mechanisms in information technology markets through effective enforcement of competition principles, limiting monopolistic practices, and economic concentration that restricts freedom of competition.",""],[1,"32","6","National Data Generation and Open Access System","The concept of data generation and availability entails providing information from various sources based on documented and updated data across all domains, enabling its storage and utilization in a manner that allows universal access.",""],[1,"33","5","National Sustainable Development Data Platform Enhancement","These criteria include having Application Programming Interfaces (APIs) in place to facilitate data usage among government entities and the public, utilizing interactive visual tools for efficient data comprehension and analysis, ensuring data availability in multiple languages, and enabling data downloads.",""],[1,"34","1","Integrated National Accounts Compilation Platform","MPED launched the integrated system, called \"Bayan platform,\" for the compilation and calculation of national accounts.",""],[1,"34","2","National Strategy for Development of Statistics","Egypt developed a comprehensive National Strategy for Development of Statistics, which aims to improve the national statistical system's capacity to generate timely and high-quality statistical data required for the country.",""],[1,"34","3","National Database Linkage and Citizen Data Integration","Efforts have been made to link national databases to unify essential citizen data such as births and deaths records, beneficiaries of subsidies and health insurance, government employees and retirees, civil status, and government facilities ... etc.",""],[1,"34","4","Sustainable Development Data Ecosystem","A data ecosystem was launched to produce sustainable development indicators.",""],[1,"35","7","National Statistical System Strengthening","The aim is for the state to adopt policies that aid in the development of a robust, comprehensive, and sustainable statistical system, ensuring the generation and availability of data, and capitalizing on the support offered by financial institutions and international organizations to reinforce data systems, as well as foster coordination mechanisms between data producers and data users.",""],[1,"35","9","Data Provision Law for Scientific Research and Development","Enacting a law for data provision for the purpose of scientific research and development.",""],[1,"35","10","Data Production and Accessibility Legislative Update","Updating legislations related to data production and accessibility, and improving the information",""],[1,"36","1","Government Database Linkage and Data Monitoring Infrastructure","infrastructure to monitor data and link between government databases.",""],[1,"36","4","Statistical System Coordination and Collaboration Mechanism","Facilitating effective coordination and collaboration between national statistical systems and international organizations to enhance data availability and ensure good governance.",""],[1,"39","2","Periodic Data and Information Provision for Legislative Process","Periodic data and information are made available for the purpose of continuously updating the informational basis of the legislative process, so that policy alternatives are realistic when presented.",""],[1,"93","1","National Data Generation and Scenario Analysis Capacity","“Data Generation and Availability” which involves the ability to analyze historical data and generate future scenarios that inform the country's plans.",""],[1,"67","9","Integrated Information System for Cultural Work","Establish an integrated information system for cultural work, enabling accurate data-driven",""]],"25":[[1,"31","8","Support for Emerging Technology Companies","Embracing emerging technology companies by providing them with financial and technical support.",""]],"26":[[1,"31","3","Economic Sector Reorganization and Competitiveness Reform","This entails innovation in production and consumption models, reorganizing economic sectors, introducing new conditions for competitiveness, and reducing transaction costs.",""],[1,"36","6","Fair Competition Policy Reform","It may also involve supporting fair competition policies",""],[1,"36","6","Efficiency Improvement Measures","increasing efficiency",""],[1,"115","1","Fair Competition Policy and Investment Diversification","advocating for fair competition policies, and stimulating and diversifying investments to enhance job opportunities.",""],[1,"120","4","Competition Policy and Regulatory Framework Reform","Establishing robust procedural and legislative frameworks coupled with adopting an effective and fair competition policy.",""]],"27":[[1,"36","5","Supportive Legislative Environment for Development Goals","A supportive legislative environment refers to the role played by parliamentary councils in enacting legislations related to development goals.",""],[1,"36","5","Parliamentary Oversight of Executive Implementation","It also involves the parliamentary oversight over the executive authority's activities and the overall performance of the state, to ensure the proper implementation of these laws.",""],[1,"37","2","Parliament-Government Coordination for Legislative Approval","Harmony between the Parliament and the Government to avoid institutional disputes between the legislative and executive authorities when approving laws and enacting legislation, as stipulated in the Egyptian Constitution of 2014 and its amendments.",""],[1,"38","5","Parliamentary Oversight and Citizen Representation","The Parliament as a Partner in Responsibility contributes to development by efficiently representing citizens' demands and scrutinizing development-related parliamentary legislations to improve performance.",""],[1,"39","1","Parliamentary SDG Performance Review Sessions","Designated number of parliamentary sessions should be dedicated to reviewing government performance within the framework of SDGs.",""],[1,"39","3","Parliamentary Committee Secretariat Capacity-Building Programme","Conducting objective technical studies for certain issues related to the proposed legislation, which requires increasing the efficiency of the secretariats of committees in the Parliament by investing in training their staff, in partnership with the private sector and development partners, to provide the necessary technical support with the aim of increasing the capabilities of parliamentarians to analyze information and data.",""],[1,"39","4","Accelerated Issuance of Implementing Regulations","Priority in the legislative agenda for draft laws related to SDGs and the speed of issuance of implementing regulations for new legislations.",""]],"28":[[1,"41","2","Educational Curriculum Update and Public Discourse Renewal","Egypt has embarked on an ambitious program to develop and continuously update its educational curricula, coinciding with calls for renewing public discourse, especially religious discourse, to enhance positive values.",""],[1,"61","4","Education Quality Improvement and Universal Access Expansion","Egypt's Vision 2030 aims to enhance the quality of education and expand access to quality education for everyone, with no discrimination.",""],[1,"61","4","Technology-Integrated Creativity and Innovation in Education","It emphasizes fostering creativity and innovation by integrating technology as a fundamental component of education.",""],[1,"61","4","Human Capital Development for Children and Youth","This ultimately leads to the development of Egypt's human capital; with a special focus on children and youth, empowering them to excel in various fields of the labor market.",""],[1,"61","5","Education Investment and Outcomes-Based Spending Reform","Increasing investment in education and linking all aspects of expenditure to the quality of educational outcomes.",""],[1,"62","1","Education Financing Reallocation and Per-Student Funding Increase","Increasing the average funding allocated to education per student, while redistributing public spending on education across different levels of education (pre-primary, primary, university, and technical education) to improve the overall quality of the education system.",""],[1,"62","2","Teacher Evaluation Incentives and Rewards System","enacting a legislation that links teacher evaluation results to incentives, and establishing a system of encouragement and rewards to foster their continuous professional development.",""],[1,"62","4","Curriculum Development for Sustainable Development Values","Developing curricula that instill sustainable development values and principles among students, whether children, adolescents, and youth, across all educational stages.",""],[1,"62","5","Education 2.0 Curriculum and Learning Materials Design","Designing curricula and educational materials within the framework of the \"Education 2.0\" system, which has proven successful at the primary level.",""],[1,"62","6","Labor Market-Aligned Education Curriculum Reform","Connecting university, technical, and vocational education curricula with the needs of the labor market.",""],[1,"63","2","International Accreditation Incentive Program for Higher Education Institutions","Developing incentive programs to encourage higher education institutions to apply for international accreditation.",""],[1,"63","4","Education Awareness and Technical Education Promotion Campaign","Increase awareness and improve societal perception of the importance of education in general, and technical education in particular.",""]],"29":[[1,"42","5","Civic Education on Rule of Law and Public Fund Stewardship","Promoting a culture of respecting the law and preserving public funds by incorporating this value into educational curricula and highlighting positive models in society.",""],[1,"42","6","Youth Civic and Cultural Engagement Initiative","Stimulating values of loyalty and belonging by bringing youth-whether in schools or educational institutions- closer to the national institutions, introducing them to these institutions, and widely disseminating cultural content to acquaint individuals of various age groups with Egypt's history.",""],[1,"43","3","Volunteer Values Integration in Education Curricula","Emphasizing volunteer work values, raising awareness among youth, and integrating them into curricula and student activities at all educational levels is essential.",""],[1,"43","5","Promotion of Scientific Knowledge and Fact-Based Public Discourse","Upholding a culture that values scientific knowledge and facts is crucial for promoting rationality in public discourse, policy alternatives, and enhancing the scientific approach in public discussions and dialogues.",""],[1,"43","5","State Institution Commitment to Scientific Values","This starts with the commitment of official state institutions to these values in their rhetoric and behavior.",""],[1,"43","5","Countering Myths and Rumors in Public Discourse","Additionally, confronting alternative narratives that promote myths and rumors.",""],[1,"84","4","Youth and Social Participation Mechanisms","Deepen political participation mechanisms for youth and all social groups and encourage youth to engage in collective and volunteer work to serve the community.",""]],"30":[[1,"46","2","Free Family Planning Services and Mobile Clinic Outreach","This involves providing these services free of charge in all health institutions and establishing mobile clinics to cover remote areas.",""],[1,"46","3","Family Planning Supply and Free Provision Budget Allocation","Allocating a provision in the state's general budget to ensure the continuous and long-term availability of family planning methods, guaranteeing their free provision.",""],[1,"46","4","Community-Based Family Planning Awareness Campaign","Increasing knowledge and awareness of the small family model through community mobilization that relies on prominent figures of fame and status who have the people's trust, with the ability to influence public opinion.",""],[1,"46","4","Family Planning Advocacy by Local and Religious Leaders","Additionally, encourage local leaders and religious figures to adopt family planning issues in their speeches, along with the continuous development of media messages based on scientific studies, opinion polls, and innovative content that deepens their impact on behavior.",""],[1,"46","5","Population Education in School Curricula","Incorporating population issues into school curricula to instill the importance of family planning in young minds.",""],[1,"46","6","Enforcement of Minimum Marriage Age Laws","Effectively implementing laws setting the minimum age of marriage and considering a harsher punishment for underage marriage.",""],[1,"46","7","Pre-Marital Screening and Counseling Expansion","Expanding the pre-marital screenings and counseling programs.",""],[1,"59","11","Family Planning Awareness and Contraceptive Information Dissemination","Increasing awareness and disseminating information about family planning services, and the availability of contraceptive methods, according to the needs of different regions.",""]],"31":[[1,"51","5","Integrated Development and Service Coordination Approach","the GoE adopted an integrated development approach through collaboration among national institutions, civil society, and the private sector.",""],[1,"51","5","Hayah Karima Decent Life Initiative","such as the presidential initiative \"Hayah Karima\" (Decent Life Initiative).",""]],"32":[[1,"54","5","Integrated Social Protection System for People Below the Poverty Line","Establish an integrated protection system for those below the poverty line.",""],[1,"54","6","Expansion of Exceptional Social Protection Programs","Expand exceptional social protection programs to include those living below the poverty line and the most in need groups, even in challenging circumstances.",""],[1,"54","7","Additional Social Protection Programs and Conditional Cash Assistance","Introducing additional social protection programs to combat poverty, and offer conditional cash assistance.",""],[1,"75","2","Financing for Vulnerable Groups","\"Financing\" that supports providing the necessary financial resources to empower vulnerable groups economically;",""],[1,"76","2","Social and Health Insurance Scheme","Social and health insurance that mitigates risks associated with unemployment, health issues, disabilities, work-related injuries, and aging, such as health insurance or insurance against unemployment.",""],[1,"76","3","Social Safety Nets for Poor Individuals and Families","Social safety nets that provide cash or in-kind support to individuals or families living in poverty.",""],[1,"76","4","Social Protection Programs for Vulnerable Groups","The pursuit of justice is closely tied to the existence of an interconnected network of social protection programs, which cater to the most vulnerable groups experiencing poverty due to various circumstances.",""],[1,"77","1","Universal Health Insurance Law","the Universal Health Insurance Law was issued in 2018, as a social solidarity system providing healthcare services to everyone without discrimination.",""],[1,"77","1","Social Insurance and Pensions Law Reform","the Social Insurance and Pensions Law was enacted with new features such as setting a minimum pension, adjusting the relationship between the pension amount and inflation rates, entitlement to unemployment benefits, encouraging incentives for insuring irregular workers, and the gradual increase in retirement age, and more.",""],[1,"77","1","Aman Temporary Social Protection Certificates","the state issued \"Aman\" certificates for irregular workers to provide temporary social protection for them and their families in the event of disability or death, serving as an interim solution until a comprehensive regulatory law is enacted.",""],[1,"77","2","Social Safety Nets Expansion and Improvement","The GoE has also taken several measures to enhance and improve social safety nets, including the food support system, targeted cash support, social housing, school nutrition programs, and more.",""],[1,"77","3","Social Protection Network Expansion and Targeting Reform","Egypt's Vision 2030 aims to expand the scope and coverage of social protection networks, enhance the benefits received by individuals, and improve the targeting mechanisms and institutional arrangements to maximize their effectiveness.",""],[1,"78","1","Electronic Database Development for Vulnerable Groups","Developing accurate electronic databases that capture the conditions of vulnerable groups and its development in society, then designing policies that enhance programs effectiveness and improve targeting methods.",""],[1,"78","3","Targeted Social Protection Expansion for Poor Families","Expand the coverage of targeted social protection programs for poor families in Egypt, with a focus on women below the poverty line and rural areas especially in Upper Egypt.",""],[1,"78","4","Social Protection Capacity Building and Conditional Cash Transfer Expansion","Ensuring sustainability for social protection programs by training and qualifying beneficiaries, along with expanding conditional cash transfer programs to alleviate the burden on social safety nets.",""],[1,"78","5","Expansion of Social and Health Insurance Coverage","Expand the coverage of social and health insurance by encouraging the workforce in both the formal and informal sectors to participate in social security systems, providing protection against the risks of aging, disability, unemployment, and others.",""],[1,"78","6","Food and Healthcare Card Distribution for Children","Distributing food and healthcare cards for children from birth",""]],"33":[[1,"54","8","Private Sector Investment Promotion for Decent Employment","Promoting private sector investments to foster the creation of more decent employment opportunities.",""],[1,"76","3","Labor Market Employment and Worker Protection Programmes","Labor market interventions that aim at implementing programs to enhance effective employment in labor markets and protect workers.",""],[1,"122","1","Worker Rights and Occupational Welfare Measures","embodies a commitment to upholding the fundamental rights of workers, incorporating safety rules, fair and rewarding wages, and social insurance.",""]],"34":[[1,"56","1","Agricultural Sector Modernization Programme","This will be pursued by modernizing the agricultural sector, improving the living standards for rural communities, increasing agricultural productivity, and investing in geographical resources across different agricultural regions.",""],[1,"56","5","One and a Half Million Acres Agricultural Expansion Project","Increasing the agricultural land area and implementing flexible farming practices as part of the \"one and a half million acres\" project, to achieve self-sufficiency in multiple crops.",""],[1,"56","6","High-Nutrition Crop Production Expansion and Productivity Improvement","Expanding production of key crops with high nutritional value, such as wheat and corn, while improving productivity and adopting new varieties and technical recommendations.",""],[1,"56","8","Sustainable and Organic Farming Support","Embracing environmental considerations, promoting sustainable and organic farming, and providing organic and mineral fertilizers and non-synthetic foliar fertilizers while rationalizing their use.",""],[1,"57","1","Private Sector Investment Support for Sustainable and Organic Agriculture","Encouraging private sector investment in sustainable and organic agriculture and food processing activities through incentivized packages and financial support.",""],[1,"57","2","Livestock and Poultry Genetic Improvement Program","Implementing genetic improvement programs to enhance the productivity of livestock and poultry.",""],[1,"57","3","Fisheries Development Investment Allocation","Allocating investments for the development of fisheries.",""],[1,"99","2","Agricultural Land Protection and Rehabilitation Measures","preserving their area can be achieved by halting encroachments, addressing land degradation and erosion, and upgrading the irrigation and drainage systems.",""],[1,"108","2","Agricultural Transport and Storage Services Improvement","Improving transportation and storage services for agricultural and food crops for the private sector, to reduce losses.",""]],"35":[[1,"56","1","Food Security and Nutrition System","Egypt's Vision 2030 aims to guarantee food provision and food security by ensuring the availability of food commodities and establishing a comprehensive nutrition system for all Egyptians.",""],[1,"57","4","Healthy Consumption Awareness Campaign","Raising awareness about healthy consumption patterns to improve nutrition levels and food quality and safety.",""],[1,"57","5","Nutrition Education and Dietary Behavior Change Campaign","Educating citizens on proper nutrition methods and the importance of changing harmful dietary habits, especially mothers, for the healthy nutrition of children, thereby reducing cases of obesity or malnutrition.",""],[1,"57","6","School Nutrition Program Expansion and Development","Expansion and development of School Nutrition Programs.",""],[1,"78","6","School Meal Nutrition Standards Improvement","expanding and improving the nutritional standards of school meals",""],[1,"83","3","Equitable School Distribution and Student Nutrition Programme","Ensuring equitable geographic distribution of schools based on the number of school-age children and providing nutritious meals for students.",""],[1,"83","4","Child Nutrition Early Detection and Parental Awareness Mechanism","Enhance children's nutrition and health by developing mechanisms for early detection of nutrition- related diseases such as stunting and obesity, and raising awareness among their parents about proper nutrition methods.",""]],"36":[[1,"56","2","Agricultural Land Protection and Food Safety Regulatory Review","Reviewing policies and legislations prohibiting encroachment on agricultural lands and address food safety concerns to achieve sustainable agricultural development.",""],[1,"56","3","Agricultural Land Preservation Policy","Formulating a policy for the preservation of agricultural lands through regular updates and analysis to agricultural soil records and incorporating the results into digital maps accessible to all agricultural stakeholders.",""],[1,"56","7","Scientific Research and Innovation for Soil and Food Safety","Fostering scientific research, technology, and innovation in soil enhancement, soil degradation prevention, and the production of healthy and safe food.",""],[1,"101","6","Legislative Support for Agricultural Land Management","Providing legislative support and activating laws encouraging technological solutions and applications, to promote efficient use of agricultural land, prevent erosion and degradation, and facilitate the division of agricultural holdings.",""],[1,"101","7","Agricultural Research Strengthening for Crop Diversity and Soil Protection","Strengthening the effectiveness of scientific research to reinforce crop diversity, rationalize mineral fertilizer usage, double agricultural productivity, increase the added value of reclaimed lands, and prevent soil degradation.",""]],"37":[[1,"56","9","Farmer Capacity Building for Good Agricultural Practices and Marketing","Supporting agricultural human development and building farmers' capacities in adopting good agricultural practices to minimize post-harvest losses and enhance marketing skills.",""]],"38":[[1,"57","7","Healthcare Sector Upgrading and Disease Prevention Initiative","Egypt's Vision 2030 aims to elevate the healthcare sector, improve citizens' health status, foster preventive measures, facilitate treatment, and proactively combat the propagation of diseases and pandemics.",""],[1,"58","4","Accessible Healthcare Expansion","This requires an increase in efficient healthcare spending across all areas of the sector, as well as ensuring accessible healthcare for everyone.",""],[1,"58","4","Healthcare System Preparedness and Medical Research Capacity Strengthening","This is besides bolstering the preparedness of the healthcare system to mitigate disease prevalence and combat pandemics and communicable diseases by enhancing the capabilities of medical research centers nationwide.",""],[1,"59","1","Healthcare Sector Funding Increase","Increasing the available funding for the healthcare sector to enhance the availability and quality of medical services in a balanced manner across different geographical regions.",""],[1,"59","2","Health Insurance Law Implementation and Coverage Standardization","Implementing health insurance laws and standardizing insurance coverage to ensure comprehensive health coverage that meets the needs from both genders.",""],[1,"59","3","Healthcare Sector Governance and Restructuring Reform","Improving governance of the healthcare sector and restructuring it to ensure efficiency and effectiveness in healthcare service management.",""],[1,"59","4","Unified Health Information System Development","Improving infrastructure and activating digital transformation to ensure a unified health information system.",""],[1,"59","5","Health Workforce and Hospital Capacity Expansion","Increasing the number of doctors, nursing staff, and beds per 10,000 people, and enhancing the efficiency of human resources while re-evaluating financial incentives for doctors, nursing staff, and technical team.",""],[1,"59","8","Vaccine and Pharmaceutical Manufacturing R&D Support","Supporting research and development related to vaccine and pharmaceutical manufacturing to achieve the highest levels of medical technology and establishing high-level medical and clinical research centers.",""],[1,"59","9","Private Sector Investment in Health Services and Pharmaceuticals","Encouraging Private Sector Investment in healthcare services, pharmaceuticals, serums, and vaccines.",""],[1,"80","3","Rural Women's Health Services Provision","The Vision emphasizes women's involvement in the workforce, enhanced political empowerment, reduction of female illiteracy rates, and provision of healthcare specifically for women in rural areas.",""],[1,"84","5","Elderly Health and Preventive Care Services Expansion","Increase the availability of services for age-related diseases and services provided to the elderly, in addition to improving health and preventive medical services for them.",""],[1,"86","4","Equitable Public Expenditure Allocation for Education and Health","Ensuring equitable distribution of public expenditure across Egypt to ensure sufficient resources for improving education and healthcare.",""]],"39":[[1,"59","6","Pandemic Preparedness and ICU Capacity Expansion","Increasing preparedness for pandemics and expanding intensive care unit capacities, especially in emergency departments.",""]],"40":[[1,"59","7","Pollution and Emissions Reduction Regulatory Measures","Activating laws and procedures to reduce pollution and emissions resulting from disease-causing production activities and limit the circulation of substances harmful to human health.",""],[1,"96","3","Environmental Legislation and Standards Update","Regularly updating environmental legislation and standards to align with advancements and abide by international environmental agreements in the energy, industry, transportation, tourism, and housing sectors.",""]],"41":[[1,"61","2","E-Learning Platforms for Remote Learning Continuity","the GoE launched several e-learning platforms to ensure the continuity of remote learning.","Ministry of Education and Technical Education"],[1,"61","3","Hybrid University Education System","a hybrid education system has been implemented in universities, combining remote learning and its technologies with traditional in-person learning in educational institutions.",""],[1,"62","8","Integrated Remote Education System","Providing an integrated system for remote education (basic infrastructure for electronic platforms and educational television channels) to cater all levels of education.",""]],"42":[[1,"61","3","Egyptian Knowledge Bank","the Egyptian Knowledge Bank (EKB) has also been launched, serving as a comprehensive repository of knowledge accessible to all Egyptians.",""],[1,"62","7","Educational Facilities Capacity Expansion","Strengthening the capacity of educational facilities (pre-university, university, and technical education) to provide adequate classrooms for all social groups in both rural and urban areas, with particular consideration for the needs of individuals with disabilities.",""],[1,"63","1","Educational Institutions Infrastructure Upgrading and Equipment Provision","Upgrading the infrastructure of educational institutions (pre-university, university, and technical levels) and equipping them with the latest necessary facilities for student training and education.",""]],"43":[[1,"62","9","Private Sector and Civil Society Literacy Participation Mechanism","Establishing a mechanism to encourage private sector and civil society to participate in literacy programs, providing schools and universities with incentives.",""],[1,"62","10","Link Social Protection to Literacy and Vocational Skills","Linking social protection programs to literacy among the beneficiaries, in addition to providing incentives for those who succeed in literacy programs (such as teaching them a vocational skill needed in the job market).",""],[1,"83","2","Literacy Reduction and Youth Employment Support","The objective is to reduce the illiteracy rates for both females and males, decrease youth unemployment, protect children, and ensure their rights to proper nutrition, education, and healthcare.",""]],"44":[[1,"63","8","Affordable Adequate Housing Access","the Vision strives to guarantee access to adequate housing for all Egyptians at affordable prices that cater to all groups.",""],[1,"63","8","Modern Infrastructure and Green City Development","At the societal level, the Vision aims to develop cities characterized by modern infrastructure and abundant green spaces.",""],[1,"64","1","Housing Projects in New Cities","The GoE has initiated housing projects in new cities to increase the individual's share of green spaces, eliminate building on agricultural land, which persisted over previous decades, and explore opportunities for expansion and better utilization of Egypt's land.",""],[1,"64","4","New Cities Expansion Programme","Expansion of New Cities in Governorates to alleviate pressure on housing and public facilities.",""],[1,"65","2","Private Sector Incentive Packages for New Urban Cluster Development","Provide incentive packages for the private sector to expand new urban clusters to generate employment opportunities and services in these areas.",""],[1,"65","6","Urban Open and Green Space Expansion","Increase open and green spaces in residential areas.",""],[1,"65","8","Urban Expansion and Encroachment Control","Halt urban expansion and encroachments on agricultural lands and prevent encroachments on the Nile River.",""]],"45":[[1,"64","3","Safe and Formal Housing Replacement Programme","the Vision seeks to eradicate the phenomenon of unsafe and informal housing, while offering legitimate alternatives that align with the development agenda.",""],[1,"64","3","Basic Services and Urban Green Space Improvement","it seeks to enhance the quality of basic services in all residential areas and increase the availability of open spaces and green areas for individuals.",""],[1,"65","4","Unsafe Housing Clearance and Building Rehabilitation","Vacating unsafe housing classified as informal settlements and transforming dilapidated buildings into habitable structures.",""],[1,"65","5","Basic Services Upgrading for Existing Housing","Developing existing housing that lacks basic services, providing sanitation services, and ensuring access to clean water.",""]],"46":[[1,"65","7","Building Law Enforcement and Compensation Legislation","Enacting legislation to support building laws, address building violations, and compensate vacated areas.",""]],"47":[[1,"67","2","Inclusive Sports Facilities Expansion","enhance citizens' awareness of sports, and provide inclusive sports facilities without discrimination based on financial capability or geographical location.",""],[1,"67","3","Increase Budget Allocation for Culture and Sports","Increase the percentage of funds allocated to culture and sports within the total state budget.",""],[1,"67","4","Governmental Cultural Institutions Capacity Development","Develop governmental cultural institutions by enhancing administrative capacities and human resources, equipping them for cultural and artistic work.",""],[1,"67","5","Non-Governmental Cultural Institutions Partnership Initiative","Enhance the role of non-governmental cultural institutions through community partnerships involving the government, civil society, and the private sector.",""],[1,"67","6","Expansion of Cultural Facilities and Heritage Infrastructure","Expand cultural facilities, cultural palaces and centers, public libraries, museums, heritage sites, opera houses, art galleries, theaters, and cinemas in various governorates and new cities, ensuring accessibility for all residents.",""],[1,"67","7","Cultural Heritage Preservation and Accessibility Initiative","Encouraging the preservation, protection, and accessibility of tangible and intangible cultural heritage, and harnessing its potential for sustainable development, creativity, and the promotion of cultural identity.",""],[1,"67","8","Youth Culture, Sports, and Heritage Education Integration","Instill awareness of the importance of culture and sports, as well as heritage preservation among youth by emphasizing them in education curricula.",""],[1,"68","6","Cultural Access and Equity Support Initiative","Provide an enabling environment for implementing innovative ideas, making cultural products available in remote and underserved areas, achieving cultural equity, and combating intellectual extremism.",""],[1,"68","9","Rehabilitation of Cultural and Sports Facilities for Accessibility","Rehabilitate all forms of cultural and sports facilities to accommodate the needs of individuals with disabilities across all governorates.",""],[1,"68","10","Sports Facilities Expansion and Distribution","Ensuring availability of sports facilities, such as centers, arenas, sports cities, and stadiums in proportion to the population in different geographical regions.",""],[1,"86","9","Cultural Centers and Youth and Sports Facilities Service Provision","Providing services of cultural centers, youth and sports facilities in all governorates.",""]],"48":[[1,"68","2","Support Cultural Industries","Support cultural industries as a source of economic strength.",""],[1,"68","3","Intellectual Property Rights Protection Measures","Support and activate measures to protect intellectual property rights including registering trademarks for cultural industries and products.",""],[1,"68","4","Cultural Awareness Promotion through Information Technology","Adopt unconventional tools to raise cultural awareness using information technology for all age groups and communities.",""],[1,"68","5","Digital Transformation of Cultural Processes","Support the digital transformation of cultural processes to ensure broad accessibility of cultural products, enhance public taste, and promote positive values.",""]],"49":[[1,"68","7","Domestic Tourism Promotion Initiative","Encourage domestic tourism as a means to enrich cultural life, instilling citizens' pride in their identity and unity within the context of cultural diversity, and leveraging Egypt's diverse environment for various sporting activities.",""],[1,"59","12","Domestic Medical Tourism Promotion","Encouraging domestic medical tourism to benefit from Egypt's natural healing environment.",""],[1,"121","4","Green and Eco-Tourism Marketing Initiative","Marketing the competitive advantages of green and eco-tourism.",""],[1,"105","1","Biodiversity Investment and Nature Reserve Tourism Development","Increasing economic return by supporting and expanding investment opportunities in biodiversity- related fields and organizing tourism in natural reserves.",""],[1,"105","2","Private Sector Investment in Nature Reserve Services","Encouraging private sector investments responsible for providing services including entertainment and education within the natural reserves, as per the laws and regulations set by the Ministry of Environment.","Ministry of Environment"]],"50":[[1,"68","8","Counter-Extremism and Tolerance Promotion Initiative","Combat all forms of bias and intellectual extremism by promoting a culture of moderation, broad- mindedness, respect for differences, and embracing change, while actively countering extremism and intolerance that perpetuate violence and terrorism.",""]],"51":[[1,"78","7","Child Protection Mechanism Strengthening","Promote partnerships among all stakeholders concerned with children's rights and enhance the child protection mechanism especially for children at risk.",""],[1,"83","2","Child Protection and Basic Services Guarantee","The objective is to reduce the illiteracy rates for both females and males, decrease youth unemployment, protect children, and ensure their rights to proper nutrition, education, and healthcare.",""],[1,"83","5","Homeless and Orphaned Children Protection and Rehabilitation Programme","Protecting homeless children, providing rehabilitation programs, and collaborating with the civil society to support orphaned groups lacking care.",""],[1,"83","5","Civil Society Collaboration for Child Support Services","collaborating with the civil society to support orphaned groups lacking care.",""],[1,"83","6","Child and Adolescent Rights Mainstreaming in Decision-Making","Support the rights of children and adolescents and considering their best interests in all decision- making processes.",""]],"52":[[1,"83","2","Disability Inclusion and Elderly Care Services","Furthermore, the vision seeks to integrate persons with disabilities into society and provide necessary care services for the elderly.",""],[1,"83","7","Accessibility and Inclusive Transport Adaptation","Facilitate the access of people with disabilities to public places and facilities, and adapt services to facilitate their movement using transportation in urban and rural areas to cater to their specific needs.",""],[1,"84","1","Smart Card and Banking Access for Persons with Disabilities","Facilitate the issuance of smart cards for integrated services for people with disabilities, and ensure their access to banking services.",""],[1,"84","2","Accessible Rehabilitation, Training, Education, and Health Services for Persons with Disabilities","Provide all rehabilitation, training, educational, and health services for people with disabilities easily.",""],[1,"84","3","Early Disability Detection and Rehabilitation Support","Educating families about early detection methods of disabilities, providing psychological, social, cultural, and physical rehabilitation for disabled children to integrate them into society, and educational and cultural systems, as well as offering suitable job opportunities that align with their physical or cognitive abilities.",""]],"53":[[1,"36","6","Spatial Justice Policy Measures","achieving spatial justice",""],[1,"84","6","Spatial and Local Development Programme","This involves targeting low-income groups, empowering communities both economically and socially, and preparing the local environment for development based on productivity and sustainability standards, to minimize the disparities between different regions.",""],[1,"84","6","Basic Services Expansion in Underserved Regions","Spatial and local development ensures making available and improving basic services in all regions and governorates, especially in healthcare, education, and employment opportunities, and increased investment opportunities in the most in need regions.",""],[1,"86","2","Investment Promotion in Priority and Border Areas","Increase investment opportunities in the most in need areas and border governorates.",""],[1,"86","5","Private Sector Rural Employment Investment Promotion","Encouraging the private sector to increase investments that generate employment opportunities in rural areas and lead to creating high-revenue jobs, particularly in the industrial and tourism sectors, as well as integrating the environmental aspect according to the nature of each governorate, to ensure sustainable utilization of local resources and enhance competitiveness.",""],[1,"86","6","Rural Attractiveness Promotion Initiative","Promoting the attractiveness of rural areas to prevent irregular migration and internal migration from villages to cities.",""],[1,"86","7","Rural Basic Services Institutional Efficiency Improvement","Improve the efficiency of institutions providing basic services in rural areas, especially in education and healthcare, to develop qualified cadres who can contribute to the development of their local environment.",""],[1,"86","8","Comprehensive Decentralization and Governorate Collaboration Measures","Implementing comprehensive decentralization measures and encouraging collaboration between governorates, leveraging their respective competitive advantages.",""]],"54":[[1,"93","1","Incentive Policies for Private Green Investment","“Financing” through incentive policies aimed at encouraging private sector investment, production, and consumption, and involving the adoption of economic models like the circular economy and the green economy to enhance added value.",""],[1,"93","1","Technology and Innovation Support for Environmental Products","“Technology and Innovation” utilizes modern scientific tools, training, and qualification to enhance environmental products and boost the competitiveness of local goods.",""],[1,"93","1","Supportive Legislative and Institutional Reform for Natural Resource Management","“Supportive Legislative and Institutional Environment” is also important for formulating necessary legislation to improve natural resource management and implement effective control measures for rationalizing utilization, in line with international standards.",""],[1,"97","2","Financial Incentives for Low-Emission and Environmental Projects","Utilizing financial incentives to reduce the tax burden on low-emission projects and facilitating financing for environmental projects.",""],[1,"97","4","Environmental Sustainability Standards for Green Projects","Implementing and activating environmental sustainability standards to increase the proportion of green projects in the national investment plan.",""],[1,"101","5","Private Sector Investment Support for Natural Resource Security","Setting a conducive environment for the private sector to invest in projects that support the security of natural resources, including organic and sustainable agriculture and renewable water resources, adopting alternative technologies to reduce industrial pollution of air, water, and soil, and expanding renewable energy infrastructure.",""]],"55":[[1,"95","2","National Council for Climate Change","the establishment of the National Council for Climate Change, presided by the Prime Minister.",""],[1,"96","1","National Greenhouse Gas Emissions Reduction Program","Developing a national program dedicated to reducing greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions.",""]],"56":[[1,"98","2","Water Use Rationalization and Recycling in Agriculture","Firstly, the rationalization of water usage and recycling, especially in the agricultural sector, which accounted for approximately 76% of water usage in the year 2019.",""],[1,"98","2","Alternative Water Source Development","Secondly, explore alternative water sources such as desalination, wastewater treatment and reuse, and rainwater harvesting.",""],[1,"98","2","Drainage Water Reuse Measures","Measures have already been implemented to reuse good quality drainage water to meet water needs, with the estimated total volume of reused water currently standing at approximately 21 billion cubic meters annually.",""],[1,"100","3","Integrated Water Resource Management and Wastewater Reuse Expansion","Developing an integrated water resource management system and expanding treated wastewater reuse to diversify supply sources, increase water resources, rationalize water use, and enhance agricultural and irrigation water quality.",""],[1,"100","4","Development of Non-Traditional Water Sources","Exploring non-traditional water sources like desalination for tourism and domestic purposes and utilizing rain and flood for irrigation.",""],[1,"101","3","Legislative Framework for Energy and Water Sector Relations","Supporting legislative frameworks regulating the relationships between the private sector and the government in energy production, sales, and water desalination.",""]],"57":[[1,"100","1","Energy Efficiency Enhancement Measures","Egypt also aims to enhance energy efficiency by developing networks and lighting systems, promoting the use of energy-saving devices among citizens, and providing incentives for the private sector.",""],[1,"95","4","Modern Technology Efficiency Improvement","improving the efficiency of modern technology utilization.",""],[1,"100","5","Electricity Generation, Transmission, and Distribution Efficiency Improvement","Enhancing electricity generation, transmission, and distribution efficiency to reduce fuel consumption and emissions from power plants.",""],[1,"100","6","Sustainable Transport and Clean Vehicle Transition","Implementing sustainable transport concepts to reduce fuel consumption in the transportation sector, and transitioning to cleaner technologies like natural gas, electricity, and hydrogen.",""],[1,"100","7","Petroleum Consumption Rationalization and Natural Gas Expansion","Rationalizing the consumption of petroleum products and expanding the utilization of natural gas as an energy source for residential, transportation, and industrial purposes, complying with local environmental standards, legislation, and international norms for government facilities management.",""]],"58":[[1,"101","1","Marine Dock and Bulk Terminal Infrastructure Development","Supporting necessary infrastructure for the development of marine docks, liquid bulk terminals, storage facilities.",""],[1,"101","1","National Gas and Petroleum Pipeline Upgrade","enhancing the national natural gas network, crude oil, and petroleum products' pipelines to optimize their utilization and reduce their emissions.",""],[1,"101","2","Local Energy Reserve Expansion and Production Increase","Boosting local energy reserves by intensifying research and exploration activities, increasing crude oil and natural gas production, ensuring supply to various consumption sectors.",""],[1,"101","2","Refining and Petrochemical Industry Development","advancing refining and petrochemical industries while gradually transitioning to clean alternative energy sources.",""],[1,"101","4","Research and Energy Investment Climate Improvement","Improving the investment climate for research and exploration, encouraging private sector participation.",""],[1,"101","4","Energy Sector Investment Attraction Initiative","attracting Arab and foreign investments to the energy sector.",""],[1,"101","4","Energy Equipment Local Manufacturing Regulatory Reform","This includes promoting legislative and regulatory frameworks that support local manufacturing of energy equipment.",""]],"59":[[1,"102","3","National Biodiversity Strategy and Action Plan","by adopting and implementing a national strategy and action plan dedicated to the preservation of biodiversity over the past two decades",""],[1,"103","3","Biodiversity and Ecosystem Conservation Commitment","Egypt's Vision 2030 is committed to conserving its diverse ecosystems, protecting biodiversity, sustaining the ecological balance of Egyptian lands and waters, and maintaining endemic and endangered species.",""],[1,"104","1","Biodiversity Mainstreaming and Species Conservation Program","Integrating biodiversity issues into both sectoral and non-sectoral developmental strategies and plans.",""],[1,"104","1","Endangered and Endemic Species Protection and Restoration Programs","Along with, establishing and implementing national programs to protect and restore endangered and endemic species.",""],[1,"104","2","Anti-Poaching Awareness and Nature Protection Campaign","Raising awareness of laws prohibiting poaching and advocating for nature protection.",""],[1,"104","5","Natural Reserves Network Expansion and Management","Developing and expanding a network of natural reserves, and prioritizing and effectively managing sites that are particularly important for biodiversity and ecological processes.",""],[1,"104","6","Natural Reserves Management Efficiency Improvement","Improving the efficiency of managing natural reserves to ensure their viability and financial sustainability.",""],[1,"104","8","School Trips to Natural Reserves and Reserve Transformation Initiative","Encouraging school trips to natural reserves and transforming them into cultural, educational, and recreational centers.",""],[1,"104","9","Traditional Knowledge Documentation and Intellectual Property Protection","Documenting and protecting the traditional knowledge of local communities, along with maintaining their intellectual property rights, as outlined in international environmental agreements signed by Egypt.",""],[1,"105","3","Scientific and Technical Capacity and Environmental Data Support","Enhancing scientific and technical capabilities to support research efforts, and ensuring the availability of data for environmental and ecological impact assessments, particularly in relation to economic projects.",""]],"60":[[1,"104","3","Responsible Fishing and Sustainable Harvesting Promotion","Promoting responsible fishing practices and sustainable harvesting techniques in the Mediterranean, the Red Sea, lakes, and the Nile River.",""],[1,"104","3","Expansion of Fish Farms Around Egyptian Lakes","developing and expanding fish farms in and around Egyptian lakes.",""],[1,"104","7","Community-Based Natural Resource Management and Environmental Product Marketing Support","Engaging local communities in managing natural resources within reserves, encouraging and training them to improve the quality of their environmental products, and supporting their marketing to create job opportunities and increase income for community members.",""]],"61":[[1,"106","3","Waste Management Legal and Policy Framework","Law No. 202 of 2020 on Waste Management and its Executive Regulations was issued to serve as a general framework for planning and preparing relevant strategies, ensuring that planning is closely linked to financing, and establishing necessary policies.",""],[1,"106","3","Extended Producer Responsibility for Waste Generators","A key policy is the implementation of extended responsibility for waste generators to handle specific types of waste, as well as clearly defining the roles, responsibilities, and stakeholders involved in integrated waste management, and ensuring the continuity of required financial resource .",""],[1,"107","1","Waste Management System Efficiency Improvement","Egypt's Vision 2030 aims to enhance the efficiency of the waste management system throughout the value chain, starting with collection methods, transportation, handling to waste reduction.",""],[1,"107","1","Waste Sector Formalization and Multi-Stakeholder Recycling Collaboration","In addition to fostering a collaborative environment between local authorities, the private sector, and civil society in managing the recycling and the transformation of the informal waste sector into a formal one.",""],[1,"107","2","Waste Management Infrastructure Expansion and Rehabilitation","This includes expanding the establishment of intermediate stations for waste storage, collection, and transportation.",""],[1,"107","3","Hazardous Waste Handling Restriction Measures","Limiting hazardous waste handling practices, such as disposing of municipal solid waste in random dumps, burning of agricultural waste, and improper disposal of waste in water bodies.",""],[1,"107","4","Waste Reduction, Recycling, and Reuse Initiative","Reducing the quantity of waste and garbage disposed in landfills.",""],[1,"107","5","Waste Treatment and Recycling Technology Upgrade","Leveraging modern technological tools to enhance the efficiency of all types of waste treatment and recycling systems.",""],[1,"108","4","Private Sector Waste Management and Production Waste Reduction Initiative","Motivating investors to handle waste management and reduction in the production processes across various economic sectors.",""],[1,"108","5","Informal Sector Formalization and Green Practices Transition","Encourage the informal sector to transition into the formal sector that adopts environmentally sound methods.",""],[1,"108","6","Community Public Hygiene Awareness Campaign","Encouraging community participation in awareness raising and enhancement of public hygiene systems through educational, cultural, media, and religious institutions, fostering a harmonized collaborative effort.",""]],"62":[[1,"107","1","Agricultural Waste-to-Energy and Safe Treatment Initiative","Furthermore, expanding the production of energy derived from agricultural waste and garbage, while ensuring their safe treatment for use in irrigation and agricultural processes.",""],[1,"108","1","Wastewater Recycling and Waste-to-Energy Projects","Expanding projects for wastewater recycling and generating energy from agricultural and municipal waste.",""],[1,"108","3","Private Sector Green and Circular Economy Entrepreneurship Support","Supporting private sector involvement and encouraging entrepreneurship in all aspects of the green and circular economy.",""],[1,"108","3","Recycling Facilities Near Sanitary Landfills","establishing recycling facilities near sanitary landfills.",""]],"63":[[1,"114","3","National Economic and Social Reform Program","This program embraces financial, monetary, and structural reforms, all aimed at bolstering confidence in the Egyptian economy and facilitating inclusive and sustainable growth that generates positive impacts on citizens by reducing poverty rates, boosting productivity, increasing income levels, enhancing living standards, and creating adequate and decent employment opportunities, while achieving financial and monetary stability.",""]],"64":[[1,"118","8","Industrial Zone Development and Industrial Complex Completion","This can be achieved through the development of existing industrial zones and finalization of the construction of industrial complexes, alongside vertical expansion.",""],[1,"121","5","Cluster Formation and Value Chain Integration Support","Supporting the formation of clusters and integrating their projects into value chains across various economic sectors.",""],[1,"121","9","High Value-Added Sector Promotion","Encouraging high added value sectors, in order to develop a conducive business environment and enhance the overall attractiveness of the country for investments.",""]],"65":[[1,"118","9","Targeted Private Sector Investment Incentive Scheme","Facilitating private sector investments in targeted sectors through offering incentives that prioritize digital transformation, green economy, and renewable energy.",""],[1,"119","4","Investment Incentives under Investment Law No. 72 of 2017","To bolster investment, the GoE has implemented various measures, activating incentives outlined in Investment Law No. 72 of 2017.",""]],"66":[[1,"120","3","Export Diversification and High-Value Export Promotion","Egypt's Vision 2030 aims to boost highly competitive exports, facilitate access to international markets, and encourage a shift towards exports with high value-added and advanced technological components.",""],[1,"120","3","Export Market Access Facilitation","Egypt's Vision 2030 aims to boost highly competitive exports, facilitate access to international markets, and encourage a shift towards exports with high value-added and advanced technological components.",""],[1,"120","3","Global Value Chain Expansion in Modern Production Sectors","Moreover, the Vision adopts the expansion of economic activities into global value chains in modern production sectors and leverages technological advancements to access new regional and international markets.",""],[1,"121","8","Export Market Access and Support System Development","Overcoming barriers that hinder Egyptian exports in international markets, while actively working on accessing new markets for Egyptian products and developing the export support system.",""]],"67":[[1,"121","2","Regional Economic Partnership Promotion","Promoting economic partnerships at regional levels, both within Africa and the Arab region.",""]],"68":[[1,"122","1","Worker Capacity Building and Social Integration Support","Moreover, it entails considerations for both physical and mental well-being of individuals in their occupational roles; as well as offering better opportunities for the workers' capacity building and thus social integration.",""],[1,"123","2","Employment Opportunity Expansion and Labor Market Formalization","Egypt's Vision 2030 aims to provide secure, decent, and productive employment opportunities.",""],[1,"123","2","Worker Safety, Rights, and Social Protection Extension","It also seeks to establish a work environment that ensures safety and security for all workers, safeguards their rights, and extends health and social welfare to irregular workers.",""],[1,"123","2","Worker Skills and Competitiveness Improvement","Furthermore, the vision focuses on reducing the size of the informal sector in the economy, all in the context of strengthening the flexibility and effectiveness of the labor market, as well as improving the efficiency and skills of Egyptian workers and enhancing their competitiveness.",""],[1,"124","3","Regulation of Overseas Employment and Worker Rights Protection","Regulating the employment of Egyptian workers abroad, and safeguarding their rights.",""],[1,"124","4","Occupational Safety and Health Awareness Campaign","Raising awareness about the significance of occupational safety and health to foster an informed society and prevent severe injuries and accidents.",""]],"69":[[1,"125","1","Financial Inclusion Expansion Initiative","The state is actively spearheading extensive initiatives to achieve financial inclusion across the country.",""],[1,"125","3","Financial Inclusion and Economic Empowerment System","Egypt's Vision 2030 aims to further enhance financial inclusion rates and achieve economic empowerment through a system that offers fair, high-quality, and cost-effective financial products and services to all segments of society.",""],[1,"126","2","Financial Literacy and Consumer Protection Measures","Enhancing financial literacy while fortifying financial protection measures for the rights of customers and stakeholders in the financial and banking sector.",""],[1,"126","3","Promotion of Alternative Payment Methods and Electronic Channels","Reducing reliance on cash outside the banking system and promoting the utilization of alternative payment methods and electronic channels.",""],[1,"126","4","Expansion of Financial Access and Electronic Financial Services","Expand financial access and provide electronic financial services to diverse sectors and categories within society.",""],[1,"126","5","Financial Institution Capacity Strengthening for Lower-Cost, Wider-Reach Banking Services","Strengthen the capacity of financial institutions to reduce the cost of banking services and broaden their reach to encompass a wider demographic.",""],[1,"126","6","Credit Facility Accessibility Support","Ensuring continued accessibility to credit facilities.",""],[1,"126","7","Innovative Financing Tools for Financial Inclusion","Activate new and innovative financing tools to seamlessly integrate microfinance customers, startups, and entrepreneurs into the formal banking sector.",""],[1,"127","2","Financial Products and Services Diversification","Diversify the array of financial products and services, both within banking and non-banking sectors, tailored to the evolving needs of customers.",""],[1,"127","3","Gender-Inclusive Banking Services","Embed gender equality principles in the utilization of banking financial services, fostering an inclusive approach devoid of discrimination.",""],[1,"136","2","Financial Literacy and Inclusion Awareness Campaigns","Organizing impactful awareness campaigns promoting financial literacy, while highlighting the significance of savings, fostering financial inclusion, and tailoring diverse financial products to cater to the needs of various savers.",""]],"70":[[1,"125","1","SME and Microenterprise Lending Expansion","there has been a substantial uptick in the loan portfolio designated for medium, small, and micro-sized projects, reaching a substantial EGP 315 billion between the end of December 2015 and December 2021.",""],[1,"125","1","Non-Banking Finance and Venture Capital Support","The state is also committed to providing non-banking financial services and introducing new financing options, like venture capital funds, to support small business owners and start-ups.",""],[1,"126","9","Non-Banking Financial Product Innovation for Low-Income Consumers","Encouraging the non-banking financial sector to innovate new financial products tailored to the needs of various consumers and citizens from low-income segments.",""],[1,"126","10","Agricultural Cooperative and Smallholder Financing Support","Financing agricultural cooperatives and providing financial support to small-scale farmers and livestock breeders.",""],[1,"136","3","Bank Credit Diversification and Private Sector Financing Expansion","Encouraging banks to diversify their credit portfolio and extend financing to the private and family sectors.",""],[1,"133","3","SME Capital Market Access Support","Facilitating increased access to capital markets, empowering SMEs to register on the Nile Stock Exchange and tap into broader financial avenues.",""]],"71":[[1,"126","1","Fintech Awareness and Promotion Initiative","Raising awareness about the importance of financial technology (fintech) and its capacity to cater to targeted financial and banking service customers and addressing their needs in a more convenient, flexible, and cost-effective manner.",""],[1,"126","8","Fintech Sector Support","Supporting fintech in financing, payment, lending, insurance, and fund transfers sectors.",""],[1,"126","11","Mobile and Internet Network Infrastructure Upgrade for Financial Services","Enhance the infrastructure and technology of mobile and internet networks to optimize the provision of financial services across different segments.",""],[1,"127","1","Cybersecurity Risk Safeguarding Measures","Safeguarding organizations, employees, and individuals against cybersecurity risks.",""]],"72":[[1,"128","3","Local Industry Deepening and Industrial Upgrading","Egypt's Vision 2030 aims to deepen the local industry and encourage technology-and knowledge-driven industries and enhance their growth rate.",""],[1,"128","3","Labor-Intensive Industrial Sector Promotion","Emphasis is placed on sectors with high labor-density potential, including chemical, food, spinning and textile, engineering, construction materials and craft industries.",""],[1,"129","1","Local Manufacturing Standards Upgrading through Technology Transfer","Upgrading local manufacturing standards by maximizing the benefits of technology transfer opportunities from foreign companies and entities operating in Egypt.",""],[1,"129","3","Industrial Zone and Complex Development","Localizing industrial activities for key products, expanding the establishment and development of industrial zones and complexes, and supporting the growth of supply chains to meet domestic demands and boost exports.",""],[1,"129","3","Domestic Supply Chain Development Support","Localizing industrial activities for key products, expanding the establishment and development of industrial zones and complexes, and supporting the growth of supply chains to meet domestic demands and boost exports.",""],[1,"129","5","Industrial Complexes and Regional Investment Incentives","Establishing industrial complexes in governorates with lower investments, while offering additional incentives for investment in these regions.",""],[1,"142","2","Industrial Land Allocation and Hub Development","This strategic allocation extends to industrial complexes like Robiki and the Murgam Complex in Alexandria, alongside other industrial hubs distributed across Egypt's governorates.",""],[1,"141","4","Development of Logistics, Commercial, and Industrial Zones","This involves facilitating international trade and establishing cutting-edge logistical, commercial, and industrial zones.",""],[1,"141","4","Infrastructure Readiness for Investment Projects","The objective is to propel economic growth, promoting both domestic and foreign investments by ensuring the requisite infrastructure readiness for projects, whether in expansive industrial complexes across various Egyptian governorates, or in new cities.",""]],"73":[[1,"128","3","Enterprise Linkages and Green Industry Transition","Furthermore, the Vision advocates for strengthened interconnections among small, medium, and large enterprises, coupled with a strategic shift towards green industries brimming with promising opportunities.",""],[1,"129","6","Industrial Resource Efficiency and Consumption Standards","Rationalizing resource utilization in the industrial sector, providing mechanisms to improve energy efficiency, and setting consumption standards.",""],[1,"129","7","Green Industry Development and Industrial Conversion Incentives","Shifting towards sustainable industry by fostering the creation of new green industries that produce environmentally friendly goods and services.",""],[1,"129","7","Conversion of Existing Industries to Environmentally Compatible Practices","Additionally, converting a number of existing industries to environmentally compatible practices, while introducing and providing relevant incentives.",""],[1,"148","4","Refinery Efficiency and Safety Upgrade","Improving the efficiency of refineries, transforming them into highly efficient economic units.",""]],"74":[[1,"129","2","Pharmaceutical Industry Modernization and Vaccine Production Expansion","Developing and modernizing the pharmaceutical industry, especially in vaccine production, in response to the COVID-19 crisis.",""]],"75":[[1,"131","2","Informal Sector Formalization Incentives Framework","The state is proactively engaged in the formalization of the informal sector, employing a multifaceted approach that includes facilitations, as well as tax and non-tax incentives outlined in the Small and Medium-sized Enterprises (SMEs) Development Law No. 152 of 2020.",""],[1,"131","2","SME and Startup Development Incentives","This comprehensive legal framework also incorporates incentives tailored for companies and establishments that contribute to the development of small, micro, and startup enterprises.",""],[1,"131","4","Entrepreneurship Support and SME Financing Facilitation","Additionally, it seeks to foster a culture of entrepreneurship, offer technical support to enhance administrative, productive, and innovative capabilities, facilitate access to credit and financing guarantees, and assist",""],[1,"132","3","Scientific Research and Innovation Support for SMEs","Directing scientific research and innovation towards aiding small and medium enterprises, to enhance their productivity, production processes, and innovation.",""],[1,"132","4","Formal Sector Enterprise Incentive Policy","Encouraging and motivating enterprises to opt for working in the formal sector from their inception.",""],[1,"132","5","MSME Public Procurement and Small Enterprise Support","Aligning public policy tools with the needs of MSMEs, facilitating their participation in public procurement, and enabling them to benefit from programs supporting small enterprises.",""],[1,"132","6","Entrepreneur Support Services Enhancement","Enhancing support services, including marketing and accounting, to empower entrepreneurs in navigating the complexities of business.",""],[1,"132","8","Micro, Small, and Medium Enterprise Growth Facilitation","Encourage a conducive environment for the growth of micro enterprises, facilitating its transformation into small ones, and small enterprises into medium-sized ones.",""],[1,"132","9","Fair Competition and SME Protection Policy","Enforcing policies that ensure fair competition, eliminate entry barriers, expand market reach, and safeguard SMEs from monopolistic practices.",""],[1,"132","10","Innovative Financial Services Expansion","Introducing innovative financial services alongside traditional banking loans, including alternative",""],[1,"133","2","Financial Literacy and Modern Financing Awareness Campaign","Eliminating financial illiteracy and raising awareness about transitioning to non-banking financial services and alternative modern financing tools.",""],[1,"133","4","Business Incubator and Growth Accelerator Dispersion Initiative","Encouraging the geographic and sectoral dispersion of business incubators and growth accelerators, particularly in priority sectors outlined in the national development agenda.",""],[1,"133","5","Startup Regulatory and Financing Support","Supporting a regulatory environment and appropriate financing opportunities for startups to develop and transform innovative ideas into tangible products and services.",""],[1,"133","7","Entrepreneurial Mindset and Self-Employment Promotion","Fostering an entrepreneurial mindset among school and university students, as well as youth and citizens, to promote a culture of self-employment that encourages the transformation of ideas and innovations into products and projects.",""]],"76":[[1,"132","7","SME Export Capacity Enhancement","Supporting the enhancement of technical and institutional capacities to elevate SMEs' contribution to exports and increase their access to foreign markets.",""]],"77":[[1,"134","1","Fiscal Sustainability and Public Spending Efficiency Reform","The GoE prioritizes achieving fiscal sustainability through setting priorities and working on enhancing investment efficiency and government spending.",""],[1,"135","2","Tax Administration Efficiency and Compliance Reform","Egypt's Vision 2030 aims at enhancing the current tax management system and increasing its efficiency, raising the contribution of real resources to total government resources, and curbing tax evasion.",""],[1,"135","2","Domestic Resource Mobilization and Revenue Diversification","That is in addition to mobilizing local resources, introducing new revenue sources, fostering private sector engagement, and simplifying rules to attract more small enterprises into the formal sector.",""],[1,"135","3","Tax System Simplification and Tax Base Expansion","Raising tax awareness and expanding the tax base by simplifying the tax system, reducing the informal sector, and increasing the contribution of SMEs to tax revenues.",""],[1,"135","4","Integrated Digital Revenue Collection System","Enhancing the digital transformation system for electronic collection of all tax types, customs, insurance, pensions, and real estate monthly proceeds in order to minimize tax evasion.",""],[1,"135","5","Gender-Responsive Program and Performance Budgeting","Extending the implementation of the gender-responsive program and performance budgeting, to ensure public spending efficiency, and foster inclusive welfare for all societal groups without discrimination.",""],[1,"135","6","Innovative Financing and Funding Diversification for State Projects","Encouraging innovative financing methods and diversify funding sources for state projects.",""],[1,"135","7","Government Expenditure Rationalization","Rationalizing Government Expenditure to generate additional resources without compromising essential spending priorities.",""],[1,"136","1","Financial Risk Monitoring and Government Guarantees Oversight System","Establishing a system to monitor, evaluate, and manage financial risks, including the issuance of government guarantees to ensure oversight of their financial impact on the public treasury and identification and early mitigation of potential risks.",""],[1,"174","1","Performance-Based Budgeting Transition","In addition to, completing the transition towards performance-based budgeting.",""]],"78":[[1,"142","1","National Road Network Connectivity Projects","the strategic execution of projects within the national road network to interconnect Egypt's governorates and establish transverse axes along the Nile, and concrete bridges as viable alternatives to ferries",""],[1,"142","1","Greater Cairo Subway Expansion","substantial expansions in Greater Cairo's subway lines",""],[1,"142","1","Electric Train System Development","the development of an electric train system",""],[1,"142","1","Transport and Navigation Control Network Improvements","significant improvements have been implemented in the control networks governing transportation, traffic, as well as air and maritime navigation",""],[1,"150","2","National Railway Network Development Initiative","In the railway sector, a comprehensive development initiative has unfolded, encompassing the establishment of a 10,000-kilometer railway network.",""],[1,"150","2","Nile Axes and Road Network Rehabilitation Programme","Simultaneously, major efforts have been directed towards the rehabilitation of the four main Nile axes, as well as the existing road network, covering an extensive 25.5 thousand kilometers.",""],[1,"150","2","Bridge and Suez Canal Tunnel Construction Projects","The landscape has witnessed the realization of significant bridge projects and the construction of five tunnels beneath the Suez Canal, fostering connectivity and streamlined transit.",""],[1,"152","2","National Roads and Bridges Project","the total number of road accidents decreased by 23.6% in 2018, totaling 8,480 accidents compared to 11,098 in 2017,[68] as a result of the National Roads and Bridges Project, implemented in adherence to international standards.",""],[1,"153","7","Railway Development for Passenger and Freight Services","Developing railways for both passenger and freight services, connecting the capital to new urban communities and industrial areas.",""]],"79":[[1,"143","3","Infrastructure Project Financing Mechanism","Several enablers contribute to achieving this strategic goal, mainly \"financing\" that ensures the necessary financial resources for implementing infrastructure projects.",""],[1,"143","3","Public-Private Partnership Legislative and Institutional Reform","As well as, the \"supportive legislative and institutional environment\" that contributes to activating modern contractual frameworks that support partnerships between the government and the private sector in infrastructure projects.",""]],"80":[[1,"144","3","Renewable Energy Expansion in Electricity Generation","Consequently, the state is committed to elevating the share of renewable energy in electricity generation, aligning with environmental sustainability imperatives.",""],[1,"145","1","Renewable Energy Regulatory and Contractual Frameworks","To catalyze investment in renewable energy sectors, regulatory, technical, and contractual frameworks have been introduced.",""],[1,"148","1","Electricity Generation Diversification and Renewable Energy Expansion","Egypt's Vision 2030 aims to diversify electricity production sources, increase reliability on new and renewable energy, develop water resources, rationalize consumption, and enhance the availability and quality of sanitation services across all geographical areas.",""],[1,"154","3","Renewable Energy Expansion","The pivotal role of renewable energy lies in being a primary source for curtailing GHG, thereby mitigating climate change effects by the activities of the energy sector.",""],[1,"155","2","New and Renewable Energy Authority Establishment","Egypt enacted legislations, leading to the establishment of the New and Renewable Energy Authority in 1986.",""],[1,"155","2","Renewable Energy Private-Sector Participation and Grid Regulation Framework","It has also played a crucial role in setting regulations to stimulate private-sector participation, in addition to the issuance of technical and contractual frameworks governing the operation of electricity transmission and distribution networks, the connection of wind farms and solar cells to the grids, as well as providing comprehensive guidelines for contracting with investors.",""],[1,"156","1","Renewable Energy Expansion Plan","strategic plans are in place to elevate the contribution of renewable energy in Egypt's electricity production mix (of the total electricity generated) to an ambitious 42% by 2035.",""],[1,"185","6","Renewable Energy Expansion for Electricity Generation","Increase reliance on renewable energy sources, targeting a 42% contribution to electricity production by 2035 in accordance with the 7th SDG.",""],[1,"157","2","Competitive Electricity Market for Renewable Energy Investment","Stimulating private sector engagement in renewable energy projects for electricity production by creating a competitive electricity market to attract private investments, through issuing and updating feed-in tariffs and net metering systems to ensure a conducive environment for private sector involvement.",""]],"81":[[1,"145","2","Household Natural Gas Connection Expansion","Since the commencement of operations in 1981, approximately 13.5 million housing units have been connected, benefiting over 60 million citizens.",""],[1,"145","3","Expansion of Fueling Station Network","The construction of 850 stations has been completed, with preparations and implementation underway for the remaining stations, aiming to reach a total of 1000 stations.",""],[1,"145","3","Incentives for New Refueling Station Establishment","To further serve the local market and enhance infrastructure investment, marketing companies are actively encouraged to establish new refueling stations.",""],[1,"148","3","Petroleum and Compressed Natural Gas Service Station Expansion Program","Continuing the program to establish service and supply stations for petroleum products and compressed natural gas, while continuously developing and expanding existing stations across the entire country.",""]],"82":[[1,"147","3","Canal Lining and Drainage Network Improvement","The canals have been lined and the efficiency of drainage network has been enhanced to cater to the agricultural and industrial sectors' requirements and combat pollution to improve and safeguard water quality.",""],[1,"147","4","Domestic Septic Tank and Sewage Connection Projects","The goal is to implement several projects to install domestic septic tanks and sewage connections, while simultaneously improving and enhancing the efficiency of sanitation services, to achieve 100% coverage in urban areas and increase the coverage rate in rural ones.",""],[1,"148","1","Water Resources Development and Consumption Rationalization","Egypt's Vision 2030 aims to diversify electricity production sources, increase reliability on new and renewable energy, develop water resources, rationalize consumption, and enhance the availability and quality of sanitation services across all geographical areas.",""],[1,"148","1","Sanitation Services Expansion and Quality Improvement","Egypt's Vision 2030 aims to diversify electricity production sources, increase reliability on new and renewable energy, develop water resources, rationalize consumption, and enhance the availability and quality of sanitation services across all geographical areas.",""],[1,"148","7","Civil Society Awareness and Water Delivery Support","Reinforcing the role of civil society to raise awareness about the responsible management of public utilities, reduce waste, and facilitate water delivery to rural households.",""],[1,"148","8","Regular Maintenance of Basic Services Projects","Ensuring the regular maintenance of basic services projects to foster continuous development to guarantee sustained efficiency.",""],[1,"149","1","Expansion of Drinking Water Facilities","Expanding the establishment of new drinking water facilities to accommodate population growth and urban expansion.",""],[1,"149","3","Sewage Network Expansion and Unsafe Sewage Practice Elimination","Extending the coverage of sewage networks, particularly in areas with pressing needs, and discontinue unsafe sewage practices to improve overall sanitation.",""]],"83":[[1,"148","2","Energy Sector Investment Promotion and Partnership Facilitation","Fostering a conducive environment to investment in the energy sector to encourage a more substantial Egyptian role in regional markets.",""],[1,"148","2","International Energy Partnership Mobilization","Moreover, attract partnerships with international, regional, and national entities, facilitating both technical and financial support.",""],[1,"148","5","Private Sector Infrastructure Investment in Renewable Energy, Irrigation, and Desalination","Activating the involvement of the private sector in infrastructure investments for renewable energy and irrigation projects in new lands, as well as expanding the construction of seawater desalination plants along coastal cities.",""]],"84":[[1,"151","1","Transport Axis and River Navigation Enhancement","transport axes: Cairo-Alexandria, Cairo-Damietta, Cairo-Aswan, and Cairo-Ismailia, along with the enhancement of locks (water navigation).",""],[1,"151","1","Lake Nasser Logistics Area Development","future plans including a logistics area in Lake Nasser to connect the navigational channel of Lake Victoria-Alexandria to the Mediterranean Sea.",""],[1,"151","1","River Transport Information Systems and Port Links","Navigational links and river ports, fortified by information systems, aim to augment the share of river transport.",""],[1,"151","2","Maritime Port Infrastructure and Logistics Modernization","New quays totaling 35 kilometers in length -with depths ranging from 15 to 18 meters- have been constructed, bringing the total length of quays to 76 kilometers.",""],[1,"151","2","Cargo Handling and Port Efficiency Improvement","This is in parallel to enhancements in cargo handling and unloading efficiency to reduce ships waiting time, better utilization of available space and storage areas by the Maritime Ports Authority, along with the establishment of logistics zones and the promotion of electronic connectivity, seeking to optimize freight transport.",""],[1,"153","2","Maritime Berth Expansion and Logistics Zone Development","Enhancing the competitiveness of maritime transport by improving and expanding maritime berths and creating logistics zones.",""],[1,"153","3","River Transport Efficiency Improvement","Improving the efficiency of locks and river routes to accommodate the movement of goods and reduce the burden on road transportation.",""],[1,"152","3","River and Rail Transport Competitiveness Enhancement","Moreover, it capitalizes on Egypt's geographical position at the heart of the world and aims to leverage the economic benefits of river and rail transport and boost their competitiveness.",""]],"85":[[1,"151","4","Airport Construction and Cairo Airport Expansion Projects","The establishment of three new airports and ongoing development projects at Cairo Airport to increase",""]],"86":[[1,"150","3","Green Economy Transport Electrification and Rail Expansion","This comes in addition to the adoption of a green economy methodology, that promotes the utilization of electricity, thus implementing the Light Rail Transit (LRT), East and West Nile Monorail, the three lines of the high-speed electric train, besides the expansion of the Greater Cairo Metro network.",""],[1,"152","3","Safe and Sustainable Transport Systems Development","Egypt's Vision 2030 aims to establish safe and sustainable transport systems to improve the quality of life for individuals and enhance the efficiency of transportation services for all users.",""],[1,"152","4","Clean Transport Transition","Gradually transitioning towards clean modes of transportation, such as electric and hydrogen- powered vehicles that do not use fossil fuel, to minimize pollution and foster a culture of fuel conservation among all stakeholders.",""],[1,"153","1","Smart and Integrated Transportation Network","Establishing a smart and integrated transportation network to offer fair prices that balance the interests of all service providers and users.",""],[1,"153","1","Private Sector Investment in Smart Transportation Systems","Moreover, encourage private sector investment in smart and integrated transportation systems.",""],[1,"153","4","Smart Transportation Applications Expansion","Expanding the use of smart transportation applications, leveraging modern technologies for managing and connecting transportation means with users and road networks.",""],[1,"153","5","Passenger Transport Service Upgrade","Expanding passenger transport services with distinctive features, such as safety, accessibility, smart, air-conditioned, internet connectivity, and time-saving.",""],[1,"153","6","Smart Car Waiting Areas and Public Transport Promotion","Providing smart car waiting areas and promoting public transportation policies.",""],[1,"153","6","Rapid Public Transportation Infrastructure Projects","accelerating the implementation of infrastructure projects for rapid public transportation, including electric trains, subways, and monorails, integrating with other means of transportation.",""],[1,"153","8","Sustainable Urban Transport and Non-Motorized Mobility Promotion","Integrating sustainable transportation principles into urban planning, and promote non-motorized transport, including walking and cycling, in small cities and neighborhoods.",""],[1,"153","9","Accessible Mobility Support for Persons with Disabilities and the Elderly","Facilitating the mobility of people with disabilities and the elderly using various transportation means, ensuring inclusivity.",""]],"87":[[1,"152","2","Road Safety Systems Improvement","the state is actively addressing impediments to road safety systems, including organizational complexities, interconnection challenges among relevant authorities and ministries in public transport, congestion on internal road networks, as well as underutilization of smart transportation systems.",""],[1,"154","1","Road Safety System Development","Developing the road safety system by raising driver awareness of traffic rules compliance and improving vehicle efficiency.",""]],"88":[[1,"154","3","Clean Air and Pollution Reduction Initiative","It also plays a crucial role in reducing air pollution and fostering improved air quality.",""],[1,"154","3","Off-Grid Renewable Energy Access for Remote Areas","Additionally, it addresses the energy needs of remote areas, distant from the national grid, while simultaneously tackling environmental concerns and energy generation sources.",""],[1,"156","3","Electrical Grid Capacity Upgrade for Renewable Integration","Improving the capacity of the electrical grid to accommodate electricity generated from renewable sources and addressing the resulting imbalance in energy supply.",""],[1,"156","4","Renewable Energy Investment Environment Improvement","Fostering an attractive investment environment for the new and renewable energy sector.",""],[1,"156","4","Energy Storage Research Collaboration","Additionally, collaborating with research centers to address the issue of high-cost energy storage, to overcome the challenge faced by the network upon increasing storage load.",""],[1,"156","5","Energy Storage Technology Monitoring and Deployment Exploration","Monitoring advancements in energy storage technologies specific to renewable energy systems like lithium batteries, green hydrogen production, and thermal energy storage systems, and exploring their utilization in maintaining grid stability and expanding their implementation once they become more financially viable.",""],[1,"157","1","Decentralized Small-Scale Renewable Energy Support","Encouraging decentralized small-scale renewable energy use in industrial, touristic, residential, and service facilities.",""],[1,"157","3","Energy Efficiency Technology Dissemination Programme","Disseminating energy-efficient technologies to reduce electricity and fuel consumption across various sectors, such as implementing energy management programs in facilities, transitioning the Egyptian market to energy-saving electrical and mechanical devices, activating energy-saving building laws, as well as converting vehicles to run on gas.",""]],"89":[[1,"159","1","National Artificial Intelligence Strategy","a national strategy was adopted which seeks to encourage the integration of artificial intelligence (AI) technologies into government operations to make them more efficient and transparent, and to use the AI technologies in various economic sectors to support the achievement of SDGs.",""],[1,"159","1","National Artificial Intelligence Council","a National Council for Artificial Intelligence was established in 2019.",""],[1,"159","1","Artificial Intelligence Education and Talent Hub","establishing Egypt as a regional hub for education and talent in the field of artificial intelligence to meet the demands of local, regional, and international markets, as well as encouraging innovation among start-ups and building the skills of youth at all levels of education.",""],[1,"160","1","Big Data and Artificial Intelligence Promotion Initiative","Furthermore, it aims to enhance reliance on big data and artificial intelligence across all sectors and promote the accessibility and development of these modern technologies for all segments of society to bridge the digital divide and ensure transition towards a digital society.",""],[1,"160","7","Big Data Integration Across Sectors","Expanding the reliance on big data across all sectors and in the decision-making process.",""]],"90":[[1,"159","2","Supreme Council for Cybersecurity","a Supreme Council for Cybersecurity was established, addressing threats and challenges in the field of digital transformation.",""],[1,"160","4","Cybersecurity Awareness and Digital Skills Promotion","Disseminating a culture of cybersecurity and raising awareness about necessary digital skills and information preservation.",""],[1,"160","5","Data Protection and User Privacy Regulatory Framework","Developing clear legislations and regulations for data protection and user privacy.",""],[1,"186","3","Cybersecurity and Information Security Capacity Enhancement","The Vision aims to enhance Egypt's capabilities in information security and fortify its ability to counter cyberattacks.",""]],"91":[[1,"165","2","National Monitoring and Accountability System","This system ensures the efficiency of operations and compliance with regulations and laws, as well as fosters more productive performance at the state level.",""],[1,"169","1","Data Generation Capacity and Financing Support","it supports providing financial resources and human capacities dedicated to the periodic generation of this data, to be available for use and analysis by specialists.",""],[1,"169","1","Monitoring, Evaluation, and Tracking System Strengthening","this enhances the quality of monitoring, evaluation, and tracking systems, particularly given the existing challenges impeding effective monitoring and impact measurement of implemented projects.",""],[1,"169","1","Government Database Integration and Standardized Indicator Definitions","These challenges are mainly tied to the weak interlinkages between government databases, low data quality, and the scarcity of standardized definitions for performance indicators.",""],[1,"169","4","Mandatory Periodic Progress Reporting Framework","Issuing a legal framework that mandates all entities to prepare periodic progress reports.",""],[1,"172","9","National Governance Indicators and Tracking Website","Developing national indicators in collaboration with the private sector and civil society to monitor Egypt's progress in governance across various areas and creating a website for tracking and monitoring governance indicators and related reforms in Egypt.",""],[1,"176","8","Local SDG Data Generation Mechanism","Activating the role of governorates and localities in generating data on SDGs.",""]],"92":[[1,"166","1","Multi-Stakeholder Development Partnership and Coordination Framework","Partnerships among the government, donors, international and regional organizations, the public and private sectors, and civil society, are foundational pillars of the development process.",""],[1,"168","1","Partnership Strengthening Initiative","The strategic goal of\"Governance and Partnerships\" unfolds into seven general goals: \"Administrative reform\", \"Reinforcing Transparency and Combating Corruption\", \"Promoting Accountability and Responsibility\", \"Empowering Local Administration\", \"Strengthening Partnerships\", \"Enhancing Regional and International Cooperation\", and \"Preserving Stability and Security\".",""],[1,"168","1","Regional and International Cooperation Enhancement","The strategic goal of\"Governance and Partnerships\" unfolds into seven general goals: \"Administrative reform\", \"Reinforcing Transparency and Combating Corruption\", \"Promoting Accountability and Responsibility\", \"Empowering Local Administration\", \"Strengthening Partnerships\", \"Enhancing Regional and International Cooperation\", and \"Preserving Stability and Security\".",""],[1,"177","1","Multi-Stakeholder Development Partnerships","By leveraging various forms of partnerships, be it financial, exchange of experiences, capacity-building, and/or participation in planning and implementation, the aim is to enhance collaboration in nation-building and shaping the future.",""],[1,"177","2","Partnerships and Development Cooperation Expansion","The state prioritizes enhancing international, regional, and local partnerships as pivotal elements for achieving sustainable development by adopting various patterns of partnerships.",""],[1,"177","2","Development Finance Portfolio Alignment with SDGs","Development finance has been aligned with the SDGs to provide a comprehensive perspective on main financing trends consistent with the state's vision for achieving sustainable development and bridging the funding gap for goals implementation.",""],[1,"178","1","International Organization Cooperation and Coordination Mechanism","This collaboration plays a crucial role in supporting integration and coordination in policy-making and implementation, providing technical support and best practices.",""],[1,"178","2","Sovereign Fund of Egypt","the establishment of the Sovereign Fund of Egypt serves as a mechanism to enhance effective collaboration between the public and private sectors, leveraging untapped or underutilized government assets.",""],[1,"179","2","Generation Unlimited Local Initiative","Egypt has been selected as the first model in the Middle East to launch the local version of the international initiative \"Generation Unlimited-GenU\" in 2022 ... known as \"Shabab El-Balad (Country's Youth)\".",""],[1,"179","3","Participatory Development Partner Coordination Approach","Egypt's Vision 2030 aims for collaboration between all development partners, to ensure concerted and consistent efforts and avoid duplication by adopting a participatory approach, in order to achieve sustainable development more efficiently and expeditiously.",""],[1,"179","4","National Partnership Database for Data Sharing","Develop a national partnership database to facilitate data sharing among all stakeholders, ensuring consistency and synergy among efforts while avoiding duplication.",""],[1,"179","5","Integrated Development Financing Map","Preparing an integrated development map for the financing needs through ODAs, as well as priority sectors and geographical regions.",""],[1,"179","6","Monitoring and Evaluation of Development Partner Collaborations","Conducting regular monitoring and evaluation of collaborations with regional and international development partners, to ensure the alignment of areas of cooperation with national priorities.",""],[1,"179","7","Legislative Frameworks and Incentive System for Stakeholder Partnerships","Developing legislative frameworks governing partnerships among all stakeholders and establishing an incentive system to foster active cooperation.",""],[1,"180","1","Participatory International Cooperation and Initiative Promotion","Egypt's Vision 2030 aims for the state to adopt a participatory approach to address regional and international challenges, where Egypt's role is anchored in proposing new initiatives and ideas, as well as contributing to the consolidation of efforts towards achieving shared developmental interests for all.",""]],"93":[[1,"166","2","Regional and International Cooperation for Cross-Border Challenges","Egypt's Vision 2030 envisages regional and international cooperation, which necessitates rigorous efforts to address cross-border challenges threatening development, such as terrorism, climate change, and emerging pandemics like COVID-19.",""],[1,"180","3","Multilateral Cooperation on Global Threats","Accordingly, confronting global threats through multilateral cooperation is a fundamental pillar of Egypt's foreign policy.",""],[1,"183","2","South-South Development Cooperation","Egypt is committed to sharing its developmental experiences and human capabilities with its partners in Africa, Asia, and the global south that share a common pursuit of development.",""],[1,"183","3","Support for Joint Arab Action Mechanisms","Supporting mechanisms for joint Arab action, both bilaterally and multilaterally, to address the challenges facing the Arab world, including development issues, political and security crises, conflicts, terrorism, as well as organized crime.",""],[1,"183","4","African Cooperation and Regional Engagement Policy","Reinforcing cooperation with African countries across all levels, considering it a fundamental aspect of Egypt's foreign policy.",""],[1,"182","4","Commitment to International Resolutions and Agreements","Committing to international resolutions and agreements signed between states and rejecting any attempt to impose a fait accompli while respecting international legitimacy.",""],[1,"182","1","Peaceful Conflict Resolution Commitment","Committing to sustainable and peaceful solutions to resolve conflicts.",""]],"94":[[1,"168","1","Stability and Security Preservation","The strategic goal of\"Governance and Partnerships\" unfolds into seven general goals: \"Administrative reform\", \"Reinforcing Transparency and Combating Corruption\", \"Promoting Accountability and Responsibility\", \"Empowering Local Administration\", \"Strengthening Partnerships\", \"Enhancing Regional and International Cooperation\", and \"Preserving Stability and Security\".",""],[1,"173","3","Rule of Law and Independent Judiciary Strengthening","Egypt's Vision 2030 aims to strengthen the principles of accountability and responsibility through the rule of law, which entails the presence of an independent judiciary that upholds justice, integrity, and equality.",""],[1,"182","3","Counterterrorism Cooperation and Threat Prediction","Egypt aims to consolidate regional and international cooperation, whether in predicting terrorist threats, exchanging information about their dangers, or pursuing those involved.",""],[1,"186","5","Counter-Terrorism Intelligence and Proactive Operations","Strengthening national efforts to anticipate terrorist threats by intensifying information gathering, launching proactive operations, detecting terrorist activities, and pursuing the perpetrators, all while adhering to relevant legal procedures.",""],[1,"187","3","National Strategy on Combating Illegal Migration","The National Strategy on Combating Illegal Migration (2016-2026) is a framework for efforts in this regard.",""],[1,"187","3","Public Awareness and Anti-Trafficking Campaign","It aims at raising public awareness of the dangers of illegal immigration and human trafficking, in addition to mobilizing necessary resources to enhance efforts dealing with this issue, as well as support development as a basis for combating it.",""],[1,"187","3","Capacity Building for Border Security and Crime Detection Agencies","Moreover, the strategy focuses on building the technical, technological, and human capabilities of the agencies responsible for detecting these crimes and prosecuting the perpetrators, in coordination with the civil police and the armed forces to secure the borders.",""],[1,"187","4","Regional and International Border Security Cooperation","Regional and international coordination and cooperation with neighboring countries to secure borders, develop joint training operations, and maximize the benefits from the experiences and programs applied in the corresponding security agencies.",""]],"95":[[1,"174","4","Court Infrastructure Development and Judicial Service Automation","Completing the development of courts' infrastructure -including ICT infrastructure- and the automation of judicial services, in addition to raising public awareness about litigation procedures.",""]],"96":[[1,"185","3","Nile Water Share Protection and Basin Cooperation","Preserving existing water resources and improving their utilization efficiency by adhering to international agreements to secure Egypt's allocated share of the Nile River waters.",""],[1,"185","3","Nile Basin Cooperation to Reduce Water Losses","Egypt also seeks to enhance the cooperation with Nile Basin countries to reduce losses in the river's flow to serve the mutual interests of these countries.",""],[1,"185","3","Water Conservation Awareness Campaign","The Vision also aims at raising awareness and promoting the culture of water conservation.",""]],"97":[[1,"145","1","Saudi Arabia Electricity Interconnection Project","Additionally, strides have been taken to initiate the electricity interconnection project with the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, aimed at exchanging 3000 megawatts between the two nations.",""],[1,"186","1","Oil and Gas Exploration and Production Expansion","This will be achieved through intensified exploration and production of oil and gas, while ensuring the security of the fields located within Egypt's political and maritime boundaries.",""],[1,"186","2","Regional Energy Trading and Cross-Border Energy Transaction Facilitation","Egypt envisions becoming a regional hub for trading renewable and nonrenewable energy, fostering broader partnerships for discoveries in the region, and facilitating cross-border energy transactions through commercial agreements.",""],[1,"186","2","East Mediterranean Gas Forum Charter and Regional Gas Market Platform","The signing of the East Mediterranean Gas Forum charter in September 2020, which establishes a regional and international organization and a platform for structured political dialogue on natural gas, constitutes a milestone in this field.",""]]}});